  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100612249-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, this precipitation method is difficult to neutralize the acid rain, and the quality of the stored rainwater is worse because the decay begins when the particles are small or floating contaminants or microorganisms mixed in the rainwater into the reservoir"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100472278-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the main feature of the conventional immersion-membrane separation method in the field of water quality, which is this field, is to circulate the water in the water tank up and down to prevent precipitation of suspended solids or decay of stored water, as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101904985-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the stirring device or the water stirrer 222 is formed so that a shaft having a plurality of blades is rotated by a driving motor so as to prevent precipitation of the nitrification solution introduced from the aerobic tank and thereby prevent decay"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102089278-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the aerobic tank is equipped with an aeration device or a stirring device to form aeration using air or agitation using an agitator to prevent decay due to precipitation of sludge in the anoxic tank and to supply external carbon sources such as methanol"}]</data>
</edge>
