  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-7510656-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "submerged combustion heaters, or other heat sources, may be used to raise water temperature as desired, such as in the winter to prevent water freezing if the aerator 106 is an outdoor pond"}, {"pat_id": "US-7527736-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "submerged combustion heaters, or other heat sources, may be used to raise water temperature as desired, such as in the winter to prevent water freezing if the aerator 106 is an outdoor pond"}, {"pat_id": "US-8105488-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "submerged combustion heaters, or other heat sources, may be used to raise water temperature as desired, such as in the winter to prevent water freezing if the aerator 106 is an outdoor pond"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100871326-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in order to prevent the water of the sedimentation basin 10 from freezing in the heat generating tube 50, the temperature is again sent to the recovery distributor 67 by the recovery connecting tube 54-1, and the heat is again transferred from the heat exchanger 64"}, {"pat_id": "US-4672990-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "despite colder above-ground ambient temperatures, radiant heat from main water supply line 2 should prevent freezing of main branch line 3 and main valve 4"}, {"pat_id": "US-4236382-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in any of the vacuum freezing processes described, an aqueous solution is introduced into a chamber which is maintained at a pressure that is somewhat lower than the vapor pressure of the solution at the freezing temperature of the solution to thereby simultaneously flash vaporize water and form ice crystals"}, {"pat_id": "US-5059228-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "referring to the processing of an aqueous solution by any vacuum freezing process, the aqueous solution is introduced into a chamber which is maintained at a pressure that is somewhat lower than the vapor pressure of the solution at the freezing temperature of the solution to thereby simultaneously flash vaporize water and form ice crystals"}, {"pat_id": "US-5080704-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "referring to the processing of an aqueous solution by any vacuum freezing process, the aqueous solution is introduced into a chamber which is maintained at a pressure that is somewhat lower than the vapor pressure of the solution at the freezing temperature of the solution to thereby simultaneously flash vaporize water and form ice crystals"}, {"pat_id": "US-5448892-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "vacuum freezing processes referring to the processing of an aqueous solution by any vacuum freezing process, the aqueous solution is introduced into a chamber which is maintained at a pressure that is somewhat lower than the vapor pressure of the solution at the freezing temperature of the solution to thereby simultaneously flash vaporize water and form ice crystals"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101244452-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the heater 610 of the heater unit 600 is disposed in the conduit 510 as in one embodiment of the present invention, the heater 610 is directly in contact with the fire water in the conduit 510, and the heater 610 can directly heat the fire water in the conduit 510, the heating efficiency and energy utilization efficiency of the fire water in the conduit 510 is excellent, thereby freezing the fire water in the conduit 510 quickly it can be heated to the above temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "based on the temperature and flow of the fluid, the control system 1140 determines whether the fluid in the fluid conduit system 1102 is close to freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-11608618-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "based on the temperature and flow of the fluid, the control system 1230 determines whether the fluid in the fluid conduit system 1102 is close to freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-4657038-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "furthermore, each of those devices are actuated in response to ambient air temperature and thus will serve to trickle water when the air temperature is near the freezing temperature of water, even though the temperature of the water in the conduit may be at a higher temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-4657038-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "since the actuation of the unit depends upon the water temperature within the conduit, the unit will only operate to trickle water when there exists a real danger that freezing may occur, thus minimizing water waste"}, {"pat_id": "US-4784173-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when freezing temperatures are sensed by the bulb, there is an outflow of water from the valve device and an inflow of water from the inlet conduit, thereby preventing freezing of water within the tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-4936114-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "sufficient aqueous ice slurry is fed to mixing tank 22 by conduit 54 to keep the temperature of the liquid therein close to, but above, the freezing point so that there is no increase in ice particle formation"}, {"pat_id": "US-7497228-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "because the temperature control valve measured a higher temperature, it would remain closed and not allow warmer water from below ground to replace the freezing water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100966852-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "accordingly, the present applicant is a technique for preventing the freezing of the water pipes by discharging a small amount of water inside the water pipes when the outside temperature decreases by the opening and closing operation of the opening and closing means interlocked in accordance with the contraction and expansion of the corrugated pipe to solve such problems"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for example, in one winter, a low temperature can cause freezing of a water pipe that supplies water from a water reservoir to a drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "according to this aspect of the