  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101611632-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as water and water vapor pass through each of the sub-chambers of the vessel 12, additional water vapor is produced and the temperature of the water vapor is raised to leave salt, dissolved solids, and other contaminants in the remaining water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101828136-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as water and water vapor pass through each of the lower chambers of the vessel 12, the temperature of the water vapor is increased to produce additional water vapor, leaving salts, dissolved solids and other contaminants in the remaining water"}, {"pat_id": "US-9102545-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as the water and water vapor passes through each subchamber of the vessel 12, the temperature of the water vapor is increased such that additional water vapor is created and leaves the salts, dissolved solids, and other contaminants behind in the remaining water"}, {"pat_id": "US-5562834-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the vaporized organic contaminants and steam removed from the top of the steam stripper are passed through a heat exchanger to raise the temperature of the stream to about 400 c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101147332-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "water pollution monitoring system according to the prior art, by providing a temperature control device inside the water pollution monitoring system so that the sensitivity of the sensor is not affected by the external temperature, and also provides a sensor cleaning device inside the sensor to improve the sensitivity of the sensor it s about making sure you re not affected by contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "US-11892393-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for example, as noted above, the rate of deposit of lead oxide on the contaminant sensor 175 is dependent on ph, temperature, conductivity, and ionic strength"}, {"pat_id": "US-6315886-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the invention contemplates in-line monitoring with sensors and microprocessors for automatic computer-assisted process control, such as ph sensors, uv and visible light, sensors for biological contaminants, temperature, etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100328970-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the circumferential surface of the hopper tank is characterized in that a constant temperature wire coil is attached to prevent freezing of the contaminants in the hopper tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101611632-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as water and water vapor pass through each of the sub-chambers of the vessel 12, additional water vapor is produced and the temperature of the water vapor is raised to leave salt, dissolved solids, and other contaminants in the remaining water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101828136-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as water and water vapor pass through each of the lower chambers of the vessel 12, the temperature of the water vapor is increased to produce additional water vapor, leaving salts, dissolved solids and other contaminants in the remaining water"}, {"pat_id": "US-4659347-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, the method according to my invention comprises the steps of (a) emitting the water in one or more jets into a vessel maintained under a pressure low enough to let part of that water be vaporized--together with accompanying contaminants--at an ambient temperature, preferably at or below the usual room temperature of about 20 -25 c."}, {"pat_id": "US-9102545-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as the water and water vapor passes through each subchamber of the vessel 12, the temperature of the water vapor is increased such that additional water vapor is created and leaves the salts, dissolved solids, and other contaminants behind in the remaining water"}]</data>
