  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "EP-0576981-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the sensor 51 also gives the possibility that when the water level in the washing chamber 21 drops, for example due to leakage losses, the vacuum blower 36 can be switched on again in order to compensate for these leakage losses and to always have a fully filled washing chamber available for washing processes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100656932-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "third, by connecting the sub pipe to the device for controlling the water level by desalination of water, it is possible to prevent the micro-leakage of the device to control the water level by desalting water by the check valve to maintain a constant water level at all times there is"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200428182-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "5 does not form a conduit in the main body because the motor is installed outside, and in addition to the water level measurement tube 220, a separate tube is not formed in order to prevent leakage of pressure from the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101729735-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "due to the coupling structure of the watertight packer 325, the water level is raised through the tubular packer 320, and the leakage of the sewage can be completely blocked"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102399563-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the remote terminal device can determine and monitor the leakage of hazardous chemicals or the discharge of wastewater in the factory based on the gate status information and the water level information of the manhole water level sensor to be described later"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3796706-B2", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "leakage monitoring calculation processing for comparing the actual water level on the day of water leakage monitoring with the water leakage occurrence water level pattern and comparing the actual water level on the day of water leakage monitoring with the water level upper limit (allowable) pattern or the water level lower limit (allowable) pattern and when the actual water level exceeds the water leakage occurrence water level pattern, it is determined that water leakage has occurred due to a break in the water pipeline , and the actual water level exceeds the water level upper limit (allowable) pattern or the water level lower limit (allowable) pattern"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985209-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "by estimating the wide water level range, it is possible to increase the reliability of controlling the water level in the water tank, and also, if an error occurs in either the pressure sensor or the angle sensor, such as leakage into the water pipe, the control device does not malfunction by the other"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101408121-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the plurality of detection sensors may be different depending on the structure or form of the cold / hot water supply device 100, and may include, for example, a water level sensor 612, cold water (hot water) temperature sensors 624 and 634, (wire or the like) sensor signal receiver 740 receives signals from the plurality of sensor sensors 640, 660, a water leakage sensor 670, one or more overflow sensors 690, can do"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3796706-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "test whether or not there is a difference between the actual water level of the reservoir b28 at the current time and if there is a difference, and the actual water level exceeds the water leakage occurrence level pattern, it is determined that there is water leakage, and the water leakage print water leak occurrence information is issued to the output processing unit 8 and the alarm output processing unit 9"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3796706-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "6, when the actual water level (d) on the leakage monitoring day of the distribution reservoir b28 has changed to the current time, the leakage monitoring calculation processing unit 12 compares the actual water level (d) with the leakage occurrence water level pattern (e)"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4297310-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "[0022] reservoir water level abnormal drop monitoring is intended to detect a sudden drop in the water level of a reservoir due to water leakage due to a distribution pipe accident or a large amount of water discharge due to a fire"}, {"pat_id": "JP-H0641138-Y2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "next, when running water is generated in the pipe 2 due to a leakage accident or the like, it rises above the overflow water level 10 in the water reservoir 8"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102149596-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the emergency monitoring terminal (120b) is operated by receiving power from the emergency storage battery (20), and information such as whether the valve is opened or closed, flow rate, hydraulic pressure, water level in each reservoir, leakage, etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985209-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "by estimating the wide water level range, it is possible to increase the reliability of controlling the water level in the water tank, and also, if an error occurs in either the pressure sensor or the angle sensor, such as leakage into the water pipe, the control device does not malfunction by the other"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101114764-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, there are advantages in that various accidents such as fire and water leakage, which may be caused by malfunction of the water level sensor, may be prevented in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102399563-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the remote terminal device can determine and monitor the leakage of hazardous chemicals or the discharge of wastewater in the factory based on the gate status information and the water level information of the manhole water level sensor to be described later"}, {"pat_id": "US-9709431-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this example, if the rain sensor indicates that there is no local precipitation, but that there are water levels above a threshold, the control system 100 may track property operations to determine if there is a problematic operation that may be causing water leakage within the property"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985209-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "by estimating the wide water level range, it is possible to increase the reliability of controlling the water level in the water tank, and also, if an error occurs in either the pressure sensor or the angle sensor, such as leakage into the water pipe, the control device does not malfunction by the other"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101676999-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "therefore, according to the present invention, it is possible to monitor the state of water leakage or foreign matter introduced into the water tank 1 by monitoring the rapid change of the water level and the water quality, thereby enabling cleaner and safer water quality management"}, {"pat_id": "US-4709723-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "during periods of high ground water levels, this leakage enabled additional fluid to flow into the tank to compensate for the increased hydraulic pressure of surrounding ground water and water saturated soil"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100323046-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and the venturi pipe (6) through the rubber ring 23 on the upper and lower outer surfaces to prevent leakage of chemicals, the venturi pipe (6) the valve 13 is located on the lower inner inclined surface, and the lock nut 15 and the vertical float 24 are coupled to the lower end of the valve shaft 14 to finely adjust to correspond to the water level of the chemical 30"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102149596-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the emergency monitoring terminal (120b) is operated by receiving power from the emergency storage battery (20), and information such as whether the valve is opened or closed, flow rate, hydraulic pressure, water level in each reservoir, leakage, etc"}]</data>
