erted into the rain gutter, water leakage during drainage can be prevented and the reliability is excellent"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4029133-B2", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "8 is a packing which is disposed between the inner periphery of 8 and prevents water leakage, 11c is a drainage hole which is an opening at the upper end of the flanged short tube 11a, 12a is an opening formed at the lower end of the outer peripheral guide plate 12, 12b is arranged inside the outer peripheral guide plate 12 and is a float portion 15 to be described later"}, {"pat_id": "US-8337121-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "while the 705 patent does teach the utilization of a rubber gasket for preventing leakage of snow, rain, or the like, this apparatus is unsuitable for utilization in conjunction with the system of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100487067-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the rainwater flowing on the road 28 in the direction of the arrow b in case of rainfall moves toward each grill 14 and passes through the pit chamber 16, the screening chamber 40, and the grit chamber 48, and then the leakage pipe 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101188389-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is also an object of the present invention to provide a sewer odor leak prevention device that can prevent the problem that sludge or debris accumulates and rainwater prevents the sewage inlet from entering the sewer inlet"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101188389-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "6 is a cross-sectional view showing a state in which the odor leak prevention apparatus of the present invention is installed in the rainwater inlet"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102216793-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as described above, after removing the collecting plate 28 and the sensor 25, when the handle 29 of the top tank 12 is lifted and lifted, the inlet of the lower tank 12 from the drain 19 of the upper tank 12 as (18) is separated, the open upper tank valve 12 is closed, so that rainwater in the upper tank 12 can be prevented from leaking"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102388770-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the inlet opening/closing plate 120 is submerged in a closed state of the upper inlet 11 due to the rainwater condition that does not require a closure, a free space provided between surrounding parts for smooth operation of the inlet opening/closing plate 120 rainwater may leak into the rainwater chamber 110 through such a method"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102408952-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the inlet opening/closing plate 120 is submerged in a closed state of the upper inlet 111 due to a rainwater condition that does not require a closure, a free space provided between surrounding components for smooth operation of the inlet opening/closing plate 120 rainwater may leak into the rainwater chamber 110 through such a method"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200322595-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "there is considerable difficulty in construction because the inlet pipe connection part or outlet pipe connection part of the receiver does not match, and if the inlet pipe or outlet pipe which is already constructed is forcibly bent and connected to the rainwater receiver, the connection part is weak and easily leaks"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200455130-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as shown in figure 10 and 11, the bollard-type hot water leak detection panel guard according to another embodiment of the present invention, it is possible to prevent rainwater from entering the interior of the housing 110 through the inlet 130"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2599727-Y2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "description of the related art normally, water leakage due to rain leakage, rain blowing or the like in an existing building indoors or at a work site of a building under construction, or groundwater in an underground building, occurs not only at the ceiling of the building, but also at the joint between the pillar and the ceiling"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100729127-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, the front end of the drain pipe 40 is fixed to the fitting groove 13 formed at the other end of the water collecting pipe 10, thereby preventing the rain and sewage leak through the joint portion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101715262-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thirdly, there is an advantage that the sinking of the ground caused by the rainwater receiver can be prevented by leakage of the rainwater due to the mortar operation finishing of the joint between the rainwater collector and the connecting pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200300524-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it can be inserted and inserted into the body to provide a pipe connection structure with a simple structure, and furthermore, it is possible to prevent soil contamination due to leakage of rainwater through securing watertightness, as well as to reduce the time and cost required for the reconstruction of the manhole"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101715262-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, there has recently been a problem in that leaks occur in the rainwater harbor connection port to weaken the ground where the rainwater receiver is installed, and furthermore, there is a problem that the sinkhole is formed due to the leakage of the earthworm"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101715262-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thirdly, there is an advantage that the sinking of the ground caused by the rainwater receiver can be prevented by leakage of the rainwater due to the mortar operation finishing of the joint between the rainwater collector and the connecting pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200322595-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "there is considerable difficulty in construction because the inlet pipe connection part or outlet pipe connection part of the receiver does not match, and if the inlet pipe or outlet pipe which is already constructed is forcibly bent and connected to the rainwater receiver, the connection part is weak and easily leaks"}, {"pat_id": "US-11629721-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the algorithms can be trained to determine whether sensor data from a system is indicative of, for example, a normal activity (a normal flush), an abnormal activity (a minor, medium or major leak), a condition, and/or an activity in the fluid system"}, {"pat_id": "US-9709431-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this example, if the rain sensor indicates that there is no local precipitation, but that there are water levels above a threshold, the control system 100 may track property operations to determine if there is a problematic operation that may be causing water leakage within the property"}, {"pat_id": "US-9709431-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this example, if the rain sensor indicates that there is excessive local precipitation, the calculated susceptibility of water damage may be increased based on determining that the likelihood of water leaking into the property is much higher"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101188389-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "7 is a cross-sectional view showing a strainer installation state in another embodiment of the odor leak prevention apparatus of the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100957464-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when rainwater or impurities pass through the movable plate mounted on the malodor prevention device, the movable plate is closed to prevent odor generated from the lower part of the sump well from leaking out through the grating"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4029133-B2", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "it is possible to prevent the water in the water storage tank 2 from leaking, and it is possible to surely switch between water storage and water discharge by opening and closing the drain hole 11c with the drain hole opening / closing lid 13"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102041291-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in order to solve this problem, a number of techniques have been disclosed for preventing leakage of odor flowing back from the sewage pipe back to the rainwater pipe or rainwater collection tank, for example, to cover oil and access holes of the rainwater collection tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102041291-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "however, only the mechanical devices installed in rainwater pipes or storm water collection tanks do not completely prevent leakage of odors flowing back from the sewage pipes, and as a result, odor leaks around sewage pipes or storm water collection tanks, causing discomfort to passers-by"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102041291-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "odor leak prevention deodorization system 100 of the rainwater collection tank of the present invention is installed in the rainwater collection tank (5)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102041291-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "operation control for a time to remove the odor by the chemical reaction by ozone, but there is a risk that some of the odor may leak around the rainwater collection tank in the early stage of operation because the time required to reduce the odor by the chemical reaction of ozone and odor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102216793-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as described above, after removing the collecting plate 28 and the sensor 25, when the handle 29 of the top tank 12 is lifted and lifted, the inlet of the lower tank 12 from the drain 19 of the upper tank 12 as (18) is separated, the open upper tank valve 12 is closed, so that rainwater in the upper tank 12 can be prevented from leaking"}, {"pat_id": "US-9828757-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "vacuum sewer systems operate inefficiently when water infiltration and inflow are present due to leaks and improper connections to storm water drains"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3983776-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "for example, the machine-learning algorithm can be trained with data provided from the control unit server 104, data provided by the smart water valve 126, and data associated with the security system 148 to predict devices that are leaking water"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3983776-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in response to providing the data from each of the devices in the monitored property 102 to the trained model, the trained model can produce a predicted device that is leaking based on the detection by the smart water valve 126"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3983776-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "should the smart water valve produce a detection that water is leaking or the trained model predict a device that is leaking water in the monitored property 102, the control unit server 104 can provide that detection and/or prediction to the client device 122 of the property owner 120"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3983776-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "similarly, the security system 148 can transmit a command to the smart water valve 126 to move the position of the ball valve 208 to open in response to the trained machine-learning model predicting no device is leaking water"}]</data>
