  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101323288-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as shown, the primary penetrating basin 230 is located side by side with the settling tank 210, to remove and remove the floating contaminants primarily in the rainwater flowing over from the settling tank 210"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100546061-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "also, in sewage or polluted small streams, contaminants are deposited on the bottom in sinking areas, lowlands, and bore areas, and when the flow rate increases during rainfall, the sewage power increases, causing the sediment to float and outflow"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100841267-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as described above, in the conventional rainwater discharge chamber, the floating contaminants 5 flowing in do not flow into the collecting pipe 3 in rainy weather, but are discharged into the public water through the discharge pipe 4 so that water pollution of the public water is ) is the cause"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102055349-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, by simplifying the structure of the permeation ditches, the efficiency of rainwater discharge is increased, and at the same time, contaminants are removed from the pretreatment water, the irrigation chamber, and the ditches, etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100823236-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "1 to 3, the screw screen 10 excludes coarse contaminants included in the initial rainwater during rainy weather and sediment contaminants deposited in the combined sewer pipe 2, and removes the coarse contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a water purification filtration layer formed on the upper and lower trench conduits to remove contaminants in rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a filtration step for purifying water to remove contaminants in rainwater formed on the upper and lower trench conduits"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a water purification filtration layer (70) formed on the upper and lower trench conduits (50, 60) to remove contaminants in rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a water purification filtration step formed on the inner surface of the upper and lower trench conduits 50 and 60 to remove contaminants in rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101382006-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the remaining rainwater is decayed to prevent the occurrence of odors or pests, and periodically operates the air diffuser to remove contaminants attached to the filtration device or the swash plate device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101653780-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the discharge line 322 directs the pollutants and sludge inhaled through the backwater drainage pump 320 directly to the sewage treatment plant or designated wastewater treatment facility to prevent the effluent from being contaminated by the contaminants and sludge"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100823236-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the bottom of the cylindrical screen, the bottom is formed with a drain hole is formed by the coarse sediment freely dropped through the contaminant discharge pipe and the vortex discharged to the sewage pipe intermediate intermediate sediment removed from the cylindrical screen"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100823236-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the initial rainwater accumulated at the tip of the screen body 11 together with the coarse contaminants and sediment contaminants may be discharged through the contaminant discharge pipe 17, which may cause a variety of problems such as a burden on the sewage pipe 4 or the sewage treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100841267-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as described above, in the conventional rainwater discharge chamber, the floating contaminants 5 flowing in do not flow into the collecting pipe 3 in rainy weather, but are discharged into the public water through the discharge pipe 4 so that water pollution of the public water is ) is the cause"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200446515-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, with the coarse contaminants and sediment contaminants, the initial rainwater accumulated at the tip of the screen body 11 may be discharged through the contaminant discharge pipe 17 to cause various problems such as a burden on the sewage pipe 4 or the sewage treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100516951-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "therefore, in the present invention, the removal of contaminants is actively performed for the building drainage during the initial rainfall stage with a high content of contaminants, and some of the contaminants are considered in consideration of the low content of contaminants for the subsequent building drainage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in addition, the present invention satisfactorily removes contaminants such as insecticides and herbicides contained in the drainage in the field, and suspended matters contained in the water falling out after the harrowing prior to planting, so that these suspended matters are flowed into the river or the like"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the treated water through which the contaminant is removed by passing through the filter medium filling tank 71 is accommodated in the discharge box 91 by overflowing through the discharge unit 90, and then introduced into the drain pipe or artificial wetland through the drainage path 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "therefore, in the present invention, the removal of contaminants is actively performed on the road drainage during the initial rainfall stage in which the content of the pollutants is high, and the filter filling tank 71 considering the low amount of pollutants in the subsequent road drainage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100750645-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "these storm receivers store the road drainage during rainfall and transfer it to the filtration apparatus to adsorb and remov