through the drainage grooves 1d and 1d into the gutter block 1 without being blocked by the covering material w placed on the lid-hanging stepped portion 1b"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100582023-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, the sewage and rainwater flowing along the road surface 1 in the state in which the floating block 20 is seated on the lid 11 flows to the drainage block 10 via the drainage hole 21 and the lid 11"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101923707-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the present invention also provides a device for continuously removing foreign matter flowing into a drainage channel together with rainwater, thereby preventing a flooding caused by blocking the drainage port with foreign matter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102016628-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "can rotate thus, by the auxiliary weight 115 alone, or by the combination of the auxiliary weight 115 and the compression spring 116, the drainage is normally closed to block the bad smell backflow, when the inflow of rainwater increases the guide plate 113 may be rotated to further open the drain hole"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102079279-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "even in this case, the rainwater drainage port 62 is blocked by contaminants and is not drained, and thus the rainwater guide unit 50 cannot return to the first position p1, and thus the rainwater containing the contaminants may not be excluded at the next rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102805058-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the grating equipped with a cover to open and close normally maintains the drainage hole blocked by the cover, and when rainwater flows in, the cover rotates to block the drainage hole, thereby achieving the purpose"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102805058-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "wherein the rotating part of an opening/closing cover that blocks a drain hole of a trap body is formed higher than the opening/closing part, thereby preventing the rotating part from being submerged in rainwater during the rainwater draining process"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102822205-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "an experiment conducted by the national disaster and safety research institute found that when a rainwater drain is blocked by trash or covered with rubber sheets, the flooded area increases three times and the flood depth increases by more than 2.3 times"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200328168-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the present invention was devised to solve the general problems of the aforementioned conventional warfare, the object of the present invention is to provide a rainwater drainage drainage that is provided with a blockage preventing means and a water removal means of the sediment, which prevents the rainwater from being clogged by the sediment at the source and also easily removes the sediment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200403834-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, the sewage and rainwater flowing along the road surface 1 in the state in which the floating block 20 is seated on the lid 11 flows to the drainage block 10 via the drainage hole 21 and the lid 11"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101923707-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the present invention also provides a device for continuously removing foreign matter flowing into a drainage channel together with rainwater, thereby preventing a flooding caused by blocking the drainage port with foreign matter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101519076-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is another object of the present invention to provide drainage and cleaning of an inner section which is clogged due to accumulation of gravels that move along rainwater flowing due to long-term use of the drainage pipe embedded in the slope of the block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102057994-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "drainage traps, such as patent literature 1, can drain rainwater or sewage flowing into the drainage pipe to the drainage pipe, and if there is no inflow of rainwater or sewage, blocking the drainage can prevent the odor generated from the drainage pipe from being discharged toward the road"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100702860-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by fitting the top plates together to form a sealed rainwater reservoir, the purpose is to reduce the overall weight according to the reduction of the cross-sectional area of the block itself compared to the storage block of the conventional hexahedral structure formed by the column integrally formed by the column"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2589989-Y2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "[0016] the water retention block for a rainwater infiltration basin according to the invention is much lighter and easier to handle than a conventional water retention block, so that its volume can be increased"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100779513-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, when the amount of rainwater flowing through the inlet 610 is large, as the main cartridge 620 and the auxiliary cartridge 630 are suspended, the extension part of the water gate 60 accommodated in the receiving groove 74 ( 64 is also moved upward to block the bottom discharge port 73 of the waterproof wall (70)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101258565-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, it is preferable that the area of the blocking plate 260 is made larger than the wastewater inlet 22 and the opening 110 to control the inflow of rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101258565-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the rainwater introduced into the rainwater chamber 10 is increased in quantity and gradually increased in water level to reach the moving induction plate 300 installed in the sewage inlet 22 and the blocking plate 260"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101923707-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the rainwater flowing into the branch valve 150 through the upper inlet 154 flows into the side through hole 1572 as the blocking member 156 rotates by a predetermined angle in the lateral direction in accordance with the control signal of the controller"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102747240-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "therefore, to block the inflow of rainwater into the wastewater storage tank (30), the above-described rainwater inflow prevention device (100) is installed in the middle of the wastewater inlet pipe (40)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102897725-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "and rainwater (2) is completed, thereby blocking the inlet (11)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102897725-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "flows in through the inlet (11), the rotation blocking plate (21) is pushed directly below the inlet (11) by the pressure or load generated, thereby allowing the inflow of sewage (1) or rainwater (2), etc., into the inlet (11)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102897725-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when there is no inflow of sewage (1) or rainwater (2), etc., the rotation blocking plate (21) moves along the inclination angle (a) to be positioned directly below the inlet (11), thereby enabling the blocking of the foul odor (3)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101881491-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "wherein the groundwater inlet pipe and the stormwater intake pipe are connected to an excellent connection portion formed on the upper side of the storage block to induce rainwater inflow"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0125999-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "junction box for rainwater pipes, characterized in that the junction box (3) has means of connection to a building block (1 ) and a space (6 or 28) provided between the building block (1) and the said box (3) in order to prevent water from stagnating and infiltrating"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100913911-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "multifunction offensive odor remover the present invention relates to a multi-functional odor removing device that prevents inflow of rainwater and sewage into the sewer of low-lying houses as well as odor blocking of the manhole, and more particularly, the lower shielding plate having a function of removing odors"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101198688-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "furthermore, existing culvert blocks, water pipe blocks, purification manholes, shore banks, fish blocks, anti-break blocks are made of ordinary concrete and have no water purification properties, so the wastewater contained in rainwater flowing through various types of blocks is intact"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200342682-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a manhole structure of drainage the present invention relates to a manhole structure of a sewage that treats sewage or rainwater, which is caused or incidental to life or business, and in particular, to a manhole structure of an odor blocking sewer that prevents odors from uncleaned sewer pipes from spreading to the outside air"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200416889-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the rainwater and sewage that did not flow into the upper portion of the trench cover 31 are diverted to the manhole 20 through the boundary block, so that the rainwater and sewage that do not flow through the trench cover 31 flow into other adjacent areas"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102635778-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, by ensuring that the direction of the coolant sprayed from the high-pressure spray nozzle is in the same direction as the sewage direction, in the case of a combined sewer pipe, there is an effect of blocking not only the sewage pipe but also bad odors heading to the rainwater pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101582931-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, according to the non-point pollution reduction apparatus of the present embodiment, the initial rainwater is effectively filtered three times or more in order from the upper grating, the first filtration member, and the second filtration member, so that it is possible to prevent the obstruction from blocking the overflow pipe and to supply the clean soil to the underground soil or the sewage pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101193342-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in order to prevent the water outlet pipe 3 from being blocked by foreign substances introduced with rainwater, the rainwater receiver of this structure has a certain distance from the bottom of the pipeline so that the foreign matter is accumulated in a wet state at all times"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101323649-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "first, if rainwater is supplied through the inlet 1 of the single finishing block 20, it is stored while maintaining the same water level in the entire pipeline while flowing along the curved pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101323649-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "rainwater is discharged to the outside through the outlet (2) of the single closing block 20 located in the other end of the pipeline while the rainwater flows through the pipeline as in the supply process"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102053107-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as described above, as the manhole malodor prevention device 100 includes the malodor preventing casing member 110 and the malodor blocking member 120, the malodor in the pipeline is prevented from flowing back and the rainwater is prevented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102053107-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, while the rain odor blocking member 320 maintains the closed state, when the rainwater rises in the pipeline due to excessive rain, such as rainy season, the rainwater flows back from the pipeline, the water level in the pipeline rises"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200475713-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the rainwater in the block is usually removed by using a pneumatic pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200475713-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "most of the rainwater is removed through the siphon principle, and only the remaining rainwater is removed by the pneumatic pump in removing the rainwater accumulated in the hull block, etc., so that the rainwater can be quickly removed and the air consumption can be minimized"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101111185-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when a plurality of purification blocks are connected and connected to a rainwater pumping station or a sewage treatment plant, rainwater is stored in the purification block so that the rainwater discharge load is reduced, so that the load of the rainwater pumping station and the sewage treatment plant can be reduced to prevent flooding and flooding"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200361466-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "bad smell intercepting apparatus of rain and dirty water receiver the present invention relates to a malodor blocking device of a rainwater receiver, and more particularly, to increase the water level and to increase the water level at the discharge end of the openable malodor blocking device such that the water pressure pushes the opening door"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200361466-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "to increase the open and close the door smoothly, and even if the water flows little by little to provide a odor blocking device of the rainwater receiver to open and close the door smoothly by the water pressure in the inclined portion of the discharge end"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101206269-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "rainwater can be sent to the vegetation reservoir 170, and the degree of purification of rainwater can be increased by passing through a plurality of prefabricated blocks 102 and 103"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101014995-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the amount of water increases, the water level sensor detects and opens the initial rainwater blocking door to remove the foreign matter from the primary strainer after collecting the rainwater from the primary strainer, filter it once more from the strainer, and then remove the foreign substance in the sedimentation chamber for final precipitation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200475713-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "most of the rainwater is removed through the siphon principle, and only the remaining rainwater is removed by the pneumatic pump in removing the rainwater accumulated in the hull block, etc., so that the rainwater can be quickly removed and the air consumption can be minimized"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200475713-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the discharge of rainwater to the siphon pipe 122 continues until the state where the atmospheric pressure equilibrium is achieved, thereby allowing most of the rainwater in the hull block to be removed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101014995-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the amount of water increases, the water level sensor detects and opens the initial rainwater blocking door to remove the foreign matter from the primary strainer after collecting the rainwater from the primary strainer, filter it once more from the strainer, and then remove the foreign substance in the sedimentation chamber for final precipitation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200311991-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "accordingly, the present invention was created in order to solve the above problems, the purpose of the present invention is to normally open and close the opening of the catchment block to prevent odor or pest backflow, rainwater or sewage inside the catchment it prevents the backflow of the sump to prevent the back flow of rats, etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200416118-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, by the odor backflow prevention panel installed on the top of the sump, rainwater is changed according to the amount of rainwater, sewage is introduced there is an effect that can block the odor flowing back through the sewage pipe"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5349271-B2", "para_id": "para_26", "text": "thus, if the water penetration hole 40h is provided in the wing-shaped vertical wall 40w of the vertical block 40, rainwater can flow through the water penetration hole 40h, so that the rainwater enters the water storage tank 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100660052-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "because of this, the block body 30 is installed in a row arrangement of the role of the storage tank for storing rainwater and the waterway line is formed so that the concentrated phenomenon does not occur even in a large amount of rain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100952605-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when the volume of the body block and the storage block having a hexahedron shape increases and the weight thereof increases, it is very cumbersome and inconvenient to assemble the rainwater storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101183691-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, the rainwater storage tank of this patent is a large weighted product, and as the size and volume of the unit body block itself increases, the construction work of the rainwater storage tank has to be corrected by a crane if it is not correctly placed at the construction position"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101248434-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "in this case, between the wall blocks 200 continuously arranged in the transverse direction to form the wall surface of the rainwater storage tank, the engaging portion of the recess portion 210 and the convex portion 220 is formed, and thus the strand wire 10 and the strand wire installation tool ( 100), the fastener 50, etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101301345-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, rainwater is circulated through the monthly circulation hole in the storage process, and a large amount of oxygen is supplied into the water, thereby improving water quality by natural purification.1 is a block diagram showing the overall prefabricated rainwater storage tank according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101857595-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, since the blocks used in the rainwater storage tank are usually manufactured as a separate product to meet the construction site, it is difficult to produce standardized blocks, and in order to use blocks smaller or larger than the manufactured blocks, there is a problem that falls significantly"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102005372-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, even when the fixed mesh filter 110 is blocked, an appropriate amount of rainwater should be introduced into the float removing tank 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102216793-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, it was configured to block rainwater flowing into the tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102505041-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, the filling pipe 52 is prevented from being clogged by foreign substances remaining in the rainwater flowing into the water collecting channel 41 of the road block 40, so that the filling pipe 52 flows into the water collecting tank 41"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102747240-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, even if a rainwater blocking tent (60) and frame (61) are not installed in the car wash section (10) of the car wash, there is an effect of resolving the problem of overload caused by rainwater flowing into the wastewater storage tank (30)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102747240-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "therefore, to block the inflow of rainwater into the wastewater storage tank (30), the above-described rainwater inflow prevention device (100) is installed in the middle of the wastewater inlet pipe (40)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100672275-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "2, the general operation of the rainwater toss is usually performed by sliding the valve valve plate 17 to the lower guide block 27 of the torsion housing 1 by the operation of the drive motor 19"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101537963-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the valve 320 blocks the inflow of rainwater when the filter 331 installed in the filter housing 330 is exchanged, thereby facilitating a smooth filter replacement operation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101923707-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the rainwater flowing into the branch valve 150 through the upper inlet 154 flows into the side through hole 1572 as the blocking member 156 rotates by a predetermined angle in the lateral direction in accordance with the control signal of the controller"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102118557-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "therefore, in the filtration device of the second embodiment including the ball top valve 35 of the above embodiment, when the level of rainwater filled in the upper portion of the horizontal blocking plate 31 is low or there is no rainwater, the