  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100673536-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for this reason, even when a large rainwater exceeding a design value flows into the rainwater treatment system according to the present invention, the pollutant having a large concentration of the contamination separated from the initial rainwater may be transferred to the second accommodation chamber 11b through the porous pipe 31 and the protrusion 50"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, the inner wall of the upper, lower trench conduits (50, 60) to form a water purification filtration layer 70 to prevent contamination of the rainwater is stored"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100733608-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "third, the internal space of sewage separation pipe is almost completely separated from the internal space of sewage culverts, which prevents the mixing of sewage and rainwater in sewage culverts in rainy weather, thus preventing stream contamination and improving the water quality of the water flowing into the sewage treatment plant"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100869158-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "rainwater flowing into the rainwater discharge pipe 140 by the above process is to discharge to the river or lake to prevent contamination of the river or lake and groundwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102141002-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "therefore, by the rainwater collecting well 10 of the present invention, the initial rainwater is discharged through the drain pipe 11, and the rainwater having a low degree of contamination can be discharged through the collecting pipe 16 to store more clean rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102076296-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the rainwater is stored in the storage tank 20 by using the drainage line 40, the rainwater is recovered cleanly to prevent contamination, odors, pest breeding, etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100681956-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the water in the rainwater inlet space 12 filled with only clear rainwater may prevent contamination of the river even if it flows into the river through the rainwater discharge unit 122"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102380491-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the above-mentioned joint method, the joint method using the color ring is not used for sewage pipes including rainwater pipes because it is difficult to fill the mortar and there is a concern about groundwater contamination and subsidence due to leakage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101384724-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "according to the present invention, during rain, the initial rainwater containing non-point pollutants introduced into the manhole can be drained to the sewage treatment plant through sewage pipes to reduce the contamination of the rivers by the non-point pollutants as well as inflow after the initial rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200300524-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it can be inserted and inserted into the body to provide a pipe connection structure with a simple structure, and furthermore, it is possible to prevent soil contamination due to leakage of rainwater through securing watertightness, as well as to reduce the time and cost required for the reconstruction of the manhole"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101323649-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the rainwater flows along the pipeline during the supply or discharge of rainwater, thereby minimizing contamination due to the propagation of microorganisms in the rainwater by maintaining uniform time of stagnation in the rainwater storage tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100895623-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the submersible pump according to an embodiment of the present invention can take in the upper rainwater of the rainwater through the intake port instead of inhaling the water near the bottom like the conventional submersible pump, it is effective to prevent contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101053877-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the submersible pump according to an embodiment of the present invention can take in the upper rainwater of the rainwater through the intake port instead of inhaling the water near the bottom like the conventional submersible pump, it is effective to prevent contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100895623-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the submersible pump according to an embodiment of the present invention can take in the upper rainwater of the rainwater through the intake port instead of inhaling the water near the bottom like the conventional submersible pump, it is effective to prevent contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101053877-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the submersible pump according to an embodiment of the present invention can take in the upper rainwater of the rainwater through the intake port instead of inhaling the water near the bottom like the conventional submersible pump, it is effective to prevent contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100739875-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the filter bag 80 is provided at 71 to filter foreign matters contained in the rainwater flowing into the sump 20, thereby removing the foreign matters contained in the rainwater to prevent contamination or clogging of sewage pipes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584236-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "thus, when rainwater is concentrated on the catchment surface 2 in which contamination by contaminants is prevented early by the titanium dioxide photocatalyst layer, the rainwater is transferred to the storage tank 1 through the catchment port 3 and stored"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101101703-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "according to the present invention, it is possible to effectively purify the rainwater having a high degree of contamination, and to variably mount the biostone storage means by the rack and the rack support frame, thereby simplifying the installation and removal in the filtration tank and the long-term rainwater filtration"}]</data>
