ium to remove the contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101391172-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and a filtration tank for removing fine contaminants in the initial storm that have passed through the swirl screen and discharging the initial storm in the state where fine contaminants have been removed through the discharge pipe to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101653780-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the filtration tank 210 is also provided with a filter means 220 for purifying the effluent from which solids contained in the storm and fine contaminants are removed from the stormwater inflow pipe 140 of the storage tank 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101741449-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the inlet tank 100 is formed with a screen box 120 to remove contaminants from the storm water discharged from the inlet pipe 110 and is formed at a lower side of the screen box 120, the desulphurization tool 130 is formed to have a flow regulating function"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "(2) since the filter which removes contaminants contained in the drainage by filtration or adsorption is installed in the treatment tank, the drainage flowed into the inlet of the storm drain flows through the flow path including the maintenance tank and the treatment tank"}]</data>
