  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101375866-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the filter net 160 may be any shape as long as it has a structure capable of smoothly draining rainwater to the vegetation filtration layer 110 while filtering the contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101375866-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, like the initial rainwater treatment device 100, the rainwater discharge reduction device 200 is a contaminant in the rainwater flowing through the rainwater inlet 250 and the rainwater inlet 250, the rainwater flows from the outside after filtering the filter may further include a filter net 260 to discharge the rainwater filtered to the vegetation filtration layer 210 side"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101323288-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "is not only to filter out pollutants introduced with rainwater to the storm pipe (5) side as well , removes low-density floating contaminants and sends them down to the reservoir penetrating portion (10c) side of the lower portion, the reservoir penetrating portion (10c) to send rainwater introduced from the infiltration vegetation portion (10b)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101273679-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the membrane module 407 physically processes residual contaminants and colloidal contaminants in the inflow water introduced from the natural vegetation digestion tank to produce reused water"}]</data>
