is method, it is difficult to completely remove the harmful contaminants that are strongly attached to the catchment surface by hydrophobic interaction, and the accumulated contaminants are gradually introduced into the storage tank over a long period of time during rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "therefore, in the present invention, the removal of contaminants is actively performed on the road drainage during the initial rainfall stage in which the content of the pollutants is high, and the filter filling tank 71 considering the low amount of pollutants in the subsequent road drainage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200358330-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the present invention actively removes contaminants from road surface drainage during the initial rainfall stage with high content of contaminants, and the contaminant content is less for road drainage than the treatment capacity in the subsequent treatment tank 20"}]</data>
