  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101014995-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the amount of water increases, the water level sensor detects and opens the initial rainwater blocking door to remove the foreign matter from the primary strainer after collecting the rainwater from the primary strainer, filter it once more from the strainer, and then remove the foreign substance in the sedimentation chamber for final precipitation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101258565-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the rainwater introduced into the rainwater chamber 10 is increased in quantity and gradually increased in water level to reach the moving induction plate 300 installed in the sewage inlet 22 and the blocking plate 260"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102008617-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "at the end of the sewer pipe (1), the sewage discharge port (2) is normally closed to guide the sewage to the sewage treatment plant through the rainwater discharge chamber (3) to block the discharge of odors and to increase the amount of sewage into rainwater that flows during rainy weather"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102773372-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "seals the rainwater receiving chamber (420) with the buoyancy of the rainwater (c), thereby blocking the fluid inflow into the casing (100)"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3466513-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in the event that the rain overflow basin 1 is busy or there is a blockage in the area of the retaining element 8, the water can thus flow from the basin chamber 5 to the basin overflow 7 via the emergency overflow 16 without being cleaned"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100841267-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as described above, in the conventional rainwater discharge chamber, the floating contaminants 5 flowing in do not flow into the collecting pipe 3 in rainy weather, but are discharged into the public water through the discharge pipe 4 so that water pollution of the public water is ) is the cause"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102055349-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, by simplifying the structure of the permeation ditches, the efficiency of rainwater discharge is increased, and at the same time, contaminants are removed from the pretreatment water, the irrigation chamber, and the ditches, etc"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3309310-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as a result, contamination in the storage space can be effectively avoided by always takes place with sinking water level in the rain overflow basin, a backflow of water from the storage space to the pelvic chamber"}, {"pat_id": "US-11298635-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "alternative structures, for example, chambers filled with porous media and underdrains, can be cost prohibitive and may fail resulting in flooding the rain garden with debris, which requires extensive clean-up"}, {"pat_id": "US-8501016-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "alternative structures, for example, chambers filled with porous media and underdrains, can be cost prohibitive and may fail resulting in flooding the rain garden with debris, which requires extensive clean-up"}, {"pat_id": "US-11298635-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the storm water pretreatment chamber prevents premature rain garden bypass of the untreated storm water due to sediment and debris accumulation"}, {"pat_id": "US-8501016-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the storm water pretreatment chamber eliminates premature rain garden bypass of the untreated storm water due to sediment and debris accumulation"}, {"pat_id": "US-8501016-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the storm water pretreatment chamber eliminates premature rain garden bypass of the untreated storm water due to sediment and debris accumulation"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101202895-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "meanwhile, the septic tank 30 has a series of decaying tanks 31, filtration tanks 32, an oxidizing tank 33, and a disinfection tank 34 so that the initial rainwater introduced into the stormwater chamber 210 can be sequentially purified"}, {"pat_id": "EP-2914779-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "wherein the dirty water chamber has an inlet for the unfiltered water and the clean water chamber has a rain water outlet (12) for the filtered water, with a cistern overflow which runs via a siphon (17) into the dirty water outlet"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100487067-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the rainwater flowing on the road 28 in the direction of the arrow b in case of rainfall moves toward each grill 14 and passes through the pit chamber 16, the screening chamber 40, and the grit chamber 48, and then the leakage pipe 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100487067-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the rainwater flowing on the road 28 in the direction of the arrow b in case of rainfall moves toward each grill 14 and passes through the pit chamber 16, the screening chamber 40, and the grit chamber 48, and then the leakage pipe 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100774588-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "of the front wall of the rainwater chamber (3) to be rotatable through the operation from the outside and a tap hole for guiding the lifting and lowering of the horizontal bar 71 of the drop preventing jaw 7 in front of the vertical spiral shaft 81 through which the drop preventing jaw 7 is capable of lifting and lowering"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101989601-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the opening and closing member 55 coupled with the lifting rod 51 is coupled to the upper storage chamber 35 when the lifting rod 51 moves upward to block the discharge port 39 to prevent the discharge of the rainwater to the outside"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100487067-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, when the rainwater collected in the pit chamber 16 reaches a level corresponding to the height of the connection hole 44, the rainwater moves from the pit chamber 16 toward the screening chamber 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100487067-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the rainwater flowing on the road 28 in the direction of the arrow b in case of rainfall moves toward each grill 14 and passes through the pit chamber 16, the screening chamber 40, and the grit chamber 48, and then the leakage pipe 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100447049-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, if the height of the wear 22 is excessively increased, this may affect the inundation of the upstream superior rain chamber 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200334419-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, if the height of the wear 22 is excessively increased, this may affect the inundation of the upstream superior rain chamber 20"}]</data>
