  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "JP-3459918-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the first conduit e1 or the second conduit e it is possible to guide rainwater and the like that have entered into the gutter block 1 through the drainage grooves 1d and 1d into the gutter block 1 without being blocked by the covering material w placed on the lid-hanging stepped portion 1b"}, {"pat_id": "US-6167916-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the rest of the large central sub-conduit 34 is typically provided for storm water drainage as may become necessary in the event of a flood or water overflow during a fire fighting event or burst water main"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a water purification filtration layer formed on the upper and lower trench conduits to remove contaminants in rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a filtration step for purifying water to remove contaminants in rainwater formed on the upper and lower trench conduits"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a water purification filtration layer (70) formed on the upper and lower trench conduits (50, 60) to remove contaminants in rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a water purification filtration step formed on the inner surface of the upper and lower trench conduits 50 and 60 to remove contaminants in rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, the inner wall of the upper, lower trench conduits (50, 60) to form a water purification filtration layer 70 to prevent contamination of the rainwater is stored"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100696883-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when the external force is applied to the sewage pipe or drainage pipe is to support the sewage pipe by the upper and lower fixed frame 20 will be able to prevent the deformation of the conduit"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101305591-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, due to the wide diameter, it is easy for sediment to settle in conduits, and there is a high possibility that sewage from rainwater tosoil may leak into the body of water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100959161-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, the storm conduit 10 may be provided with a plurality of overflow wear (11, 12, 13), if necessary, the front side of each overflow wear (11) (12) (13) as a settlement 20 a gate is installed to allow initial rainwater to flow in"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101173254-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by preventing the rainwater from flowing into the sewer conduit 20 by the rotation of the wear 40, it is possible to maintain a constant treatment capacity of the sewage treatment plant by adjusting the inflow amount into the sewage treatment plant, thereby maintaining excellent sewage treatment quality"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101946554-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, at the time of rainfall, the stormwater flows through the stormwater conduit (40), and the initial stormwater is transferred to the climatic site (50) side, and the continuous stormwater flows into the river while overflowing the swimwear (41)"}]</data>
</edge>
