<edge source="conduit" target="stream">
  <data key="d1">8</data>
  <data key="d2">due to</data>
  <data key="d3">["US-6121179-A", "US-5044836-A", "US-5551472-A"]</data>
  <data key="d4">["cause", "due to", "therefore", "via"]</data>
  <data key="d5">["conduit", "time", "blockage", "valve", "system", "rate", "exchanger", "solid", "contaminant", "gpm", "pressure", "stream", "end", "laboratory", "vacuum", "carbon", "mixture", "use", "response", "problem", "reactor", "embodiment", "amount", "product", "water", "particle", "fluid", "plugging", "waterlogging", "contact", "condition", "manner", "oxidation", "reaction", "erosion"]</data>
  <data key="d6">["activate", "have", "contaminate", "adapt", "cycle", "base", "contain", "adjust", "occur", "reduce", "open", "oxidize", "conduct", "prevent", "cause", "unwaterlogge", "remove", "leave", "flow", "tend", "be", "heat", "locate", "introduce"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-5044836-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "because the valve opens in response to differential pressure based upon the vacuum pressure condition in the conduit immediately downstream of the valve, if that vacuum pressure is too low due to waterlogging blockage of the conduit, the valve will not cycle to introduce atmospheric pressure into the conduit, thereby preventing the conduit from automatically unwaterlogging itself over time"}, {"pat_id": "US-6121179-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a substantially contaminant free water stream is introduced into the system via conduit 213"}, {"pat_id": "US-6121179-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the effluent stream from reactor 222, 230, and/or 240, containing a mixture of organic contaminants in water, is preferably conducted to heat exchanger 216 via conduit 248"}, {"pat_id": "US-6121179-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a substantially contaminant free water stream is preferably introduced into the system via conduit 309"}, {"pat_id": "US-6121179-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the effluent stream is preferably conducted via conduit 654 to an oxidation reactor where the organic contaminants removed from the activated carbon particles are oxidized"}, {"pat_id": "US-6121179-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this manner the amount of time that the activated carbon particles are in contact with the contaminated water may be adjusted such that the organic contaminants are substantially removed from the contaminated water prior to the water stream leaving the reactor via conduit 726"}, {"pat_id": "US-6121179-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "preferably conduit 450 is located near the bottom end of second conduit 420 such that oxidation occurs and thereby tends to heat the stream and cause reaction products to flow upwardly through second conduit 420"}, {"pat_id": "US-5551472-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, in one embodiment the system is adapted to reduce the pressure when the rate of fluid flowing through the first conduit 4 is less than about 7-10 gpm, and, alternately, less than about 0.25-0.50 gpm during use (e.g., for laboratory systems, which tend to have severe plugging and/or erosion problems when reducing the pressure of relatively high fluid streams containing solids)"}]</data>
</edge>
<edge source="conduit" target="subsidence">
  <data key="d1">4</data>
  <data key="d2">due to</data>
  <data key="d3">["KR-100810555-B1", "KR-102014763-B1"]</data>
  <data key="d4">["due to"]</data>
  <data key="d5">["conduit", "fluctuation", "defect", "variation", "pressure", "pvc", "sewage", "pipeline", "pipe", "separation", "subsidence", "ground", "cracking", "aging", "breakage", "earth", "disconnection", "ageing", "connection"]</data>
  <data key="d6">["mean", "have"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100810555-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in general, underground pipelines, such as concrete pipes, pvc pipes, and conduits, have defects such as cracking, breakage, or separation of connections due to ageing of the pipe itself, subsidence of the underground ground, or variations in earth pressure from the ground"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102014763-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "here, structural defects in sewage conduits mean defects such as cracking, breakage, or disconnection due to aging of the pipe itself, subsidence of underground ground or fluctuations in earth pressure from the ground"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100810555-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in general, underground pipelines, such as concrete pipes, pvc pipes, and conduits, have defects such as cracking, breakage, or separation of connections due to ageing of the pipe itself, subsidence of the underground ground, or variations in earth pressure from the ground"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102014763-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "here, structural defects in sewage conduits mean defects such as cracking, breakage, or disconnection due to aging of the pipe itself, subsidence of underground ground or fluctuations in earth pressure from the ground"}]</data>
</edge>
