  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-10927539-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "such sediments accumulate over time, often to the point of greatly impeding flow through such storm drain conduits so that subsequent storm runoff may be blocked to the point of backing up, leaving the storm drain conduits ineffective"}, {"pat_id": "US-4523875-A", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in some situations it is desirable to install a check valve in the storm drain line at the location of the manhole to prevent the storm drain line from backing up into the building s footer drain line system"}, {"pat_id": "US-4523875-A", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in situations where there is a continuing problem with the storm drain line backing up, a check valve is preferably installed in the storm drain line to prevent it from backing up"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200148426-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "due to this, various flies and mosquitoes inhabited in the sewer pipe are blocked by the blocking plates 6 installed on the outer wall surfaces of the waste collection container 4 of the storm drainage tank 1 for roads, thereby preventing passage"}, {"pat_id": "US-10927539-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "such sediments accumulate over time, often to the point of greatly impeding flow through such storm drain conduits so that subsequent storm runoff may be blocked to the point of backing up, leaving the storm drain conduits ineffective"}, {"pat_id": "US-6334953-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the flaps enable excess water from the runoff water flow to drain from the filter bag as the filter bag becomes filled with silt and other debris to prevent a back-up or blockage of runoff water within the discharge pipe of the storm water discharge system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100750645-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "these storm receivers store the road drainage during rainfall and transfer it to the filtration apparatus to adsorb and remove contaminants contained in the road drainage, and then discharge only the treated water to the sewer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "(2) since the filter which removes contaminants contained in the drainage by filtration or adsorption is installed in the treatment tank, the drainage flowed into the inlet of the storm drain flows through the flow path including the maintenance tank and the treatment tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-8961793-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "further, storm drains often are designed to not enter conventional wastewater treatment plants and directly enter open streams or the oceans, resulting in widespread outbreaks of disease, heavy metals contamination, and suspended solids, which adversely affect wildlife and human beings"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100842368-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "here, the bottom of the dust collecting container 40 is preferably located below the height of the rainwater drainage pipe 12, the height of the deposit accumulated on the bottom of the dust collecting container 40 is the maximum to prevent the discharge of the deposit it is good not to exceed the height of the storm drain pipe (12)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100842368-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this is because the sediment is not collected and can be continuously suspended by the cyclone phenomenon to be deposited in the storm drain pipe 12"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101822469-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "further, since the initial stormwater treatment apparatus and the drain port 100 can be easily attached and detached, the effect of facilitating the removal of foreign substances deposited in the initial stormwater treatment apparatus is added"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101822469-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in such a configuration, since the impurities deposited at the time of detaching the initial stormwater treatment apparatus from the drainage port 100 are separated from the drainage port 100 together with the initial stormwater treatment apparatus while being stored in the impregnation sedimentation section 900, it is possible to prevent the contaminants from flowing into the drain port 100"}, {"pat_id": "US-10927539-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the costs for hauling clean water to storm drain conduit cleaning sites and for hauling away dirty water and the materials removed from the storm drain conduits are significant"}, {"pat_id": "US-10927539-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "such sediments accumulate over time, often to the point of greatly impeding flow through such storm drain conduits so that subsequent storm runoff may be blocked to the point of backing up, leaving the storm drain conduits ineffective"}, {"pat_id": "US-8277646-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "such solutions, however, often can be ineffective at protecting and preventing dirt and debris from entering the storm water drainage system"}, {"pat_id": "US-10927539-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "such trucks can also present problems for traffic in the vicinity and can cause undesirable wear and tear on streets and highways where storm drain conduits are being cleaned"}, {"pat_id": "US-10927539-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "such trucks can also present problems for traffic in the vicinity and can cause undesirable wear and tear on streets and highways where storm drain conduits are being cleaned"}]</data>
</edge>
