  <data key="d6">["change", "have", "compare", "discuss", "provide", "activate", "freeze", "should", "monitor", "remain", "block", "discharge", "minimize", "maintain", "detect", "drive", "achieve", "accord", "allow", "say", "end", "steam", "utilize", "permeate", "configure", "occur", "reach", "go", "determine", "perform", "open", "use", "connect", "seep", "supply", "cause", "prevent", "become", "cool", "favor", "winterize", "employ", "exit", "dissolve", "leak", "produce", "build up", "expose", "collect", "space", "drain", "lower", "relate", "check", "be", "thaw", "tube", "sense", "approach", "begin", "see"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100439863-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, in the conventional washing machine generating apparatus 200 of the washing machine, the washing rate is lowered in the winter when low-temperature tap water is supplied, while a part of the electrolyte that is not dissolved is collected around the drain hole 101 to block drainage"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "optionally wherein the drain blockage is determined by the controller (142) when the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor (414) is about the same as the temperature reading of the second temperature sensor (418)"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the controller 142 is further configured to compare the temperature readings of the first, second, and third temperature sensors 114, 118, 122 to determine whether an error has occurred in the water heater 10 (e.g., leakage, drain blockage), as further discussed below"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "if the temperature of condensate is not equal to the temperature of flue gases at intermediate section 66, the controller 142 determines at box 230 that there is no drain blockage, and returns to decision point 220"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "alternatively, the temperature readings of the first temperature sensor 414 during the heating mode may also be used to determine a drain blockage"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in particular, when the temperature readings of the first temperature sensor 414 decrease toward the minimum temperature limit 682 during the heating mode, the controller will determine that there is a drain blockage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200302627-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "an anti-freezing-burst type water meter the present invention relates to a water meter, and more particularly to a freeze-proof water meter having a drain portion for discharging water in accordance with the temperature drop in the lower portion of the water meter to prevent freezing caused by the temperature drop in the winter season"}, {"pat_id": "US-4213830-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the low temperature evaporation of the waste water drain flows, which become more and more concentrated further prevents the danger of corrosion damage and of incrustation since both phenomena are favored by elevated temperatures and concentrations"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102031231-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "15, 2002)the present invention provides a drainage outlet with an inner cylinder and an outer cylinder to minimize heat transfer of the hot temperature of the waste, and the inner cylinder is spaced from the outer cylinder so that the heat transfer of the outer cylinder is not performed, so that the gap due to thermal deformation of the outer cylinder is achieved"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for example, in one winter, a low temperature can cause freezing of a water pipe that supplies water from a water reservoir to a drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "according to this aspect of the present invention, the water supply control device checks the outside air temperature sensed by the temperature sensor and intermittently drives the pump to prevent freezing of the water supply pipe supplying water to the water tank of the drain"}, {"pat_id": "US-4313452-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the lower end of the exterior thaw tube 32 thus thaws quickly and also freezes quickly, which provides a fast refreezing of the apparatus and reopening of the drain opening 30 should the ambient temperature, after only a short period of thaw, again go below freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-4763682-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the valve closing element of this patent is caused to open said valve and allow the drainage of fluid from a connected pipe in response to temperatures approaching the freezing point"}, {"pat_id": "US-4763682-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is thus seen that it would be desirable to have a simple, inexpensive system for draining water lines at the approach of freezing temperatures, and in which the activating mechanism is maintained out of contact with the fluid both during and after its activation"}, {"pat_id": "US-6763845-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus a subject water utilizing device (e.g., an evaporative cooler and its associated piping system) and certain freezing temperature exposed-portions of applicant s device are drained and thus winterized"}, {"pat_id": "US-4213830-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the low temperature evaporation of the waste water drain flows, which become more and more concentrated further prevents the danger of corrosion damage and of incrustation since both phenomena are favored by elevated temperatures and concentrations"}, {"pat_id": "US-4922233-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "monitoring systems presently used to monitor the condition of a drain valve and employing differential temperature sensors are ineffective or insufficient for a number of reasons"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the controller 142 is further configured to compare the temperature readings of the first, second, and third temperature sensors 114, 118, 122 to determine whether an error has occurred in the water heater 10 (e.g., leakage, drain blockage), as further discussed below"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "rather, the first temperature sensor 414 may be detecting a temperature of the residual condensate produced during the heating mode that has already begun to cool to a lower temperature (i.e., temperature lower than the leaking water) within the drain line 394"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the wait period 695 ends when the leaking water has reached a predetermined water level in the drain pipe 394, and the leaking water is then able to exit through the drain line 398 past the first temperature sensor 414"}, {"pat_id": "US-9752787-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the drain pipe allows for any water that may build up in, or leak into, the valve box to drain away before it can change to steam under the high temperature conditions and cause damage"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the controller 142 is further configured to compare the temperature readings of the first, second, and third temperature sensors 114, 118, 122 to determine whether an error has occurred in the water heater 10 (e.g., leakage, drain blockage), as further discussed below"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200498205-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, in the winter, if the permeated water that seeps into the pavement layer of the bridge deck is not drained quickly and remains, it freezes due to the low temperature, causing freezing and rupture of the pavement layer"}]</data>
</edge>
