7-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "to avoid such unwanted fluctuations in temperature, the increased surface area, or contact area of the chambers 447 provides a heat exchanger interface between the fluid and the material that forms the modified inlet block 444 and thereby minimize changes in fluid temperature as the fluid moves along the surface of the modified inlet block 444"}, {"pat_id": "EP-1218293-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "also, the air-cooler 25 will ensure that incoming raw water cannot be heated within the heat exchanger 18 to a temperature which would induce premature precipitation of dissolved solids in the incoming raw water, and thus lead to ultimate blockage inside the heat exchanger"}, {"pat_id": "EP-1228003-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "also, the air-cooler 25 will ensure that incoming raw water cannot be heated within the heat exchanger 18 to a temperature which would induce premature precipitation of dissolved solids in the incoming raw water, and thus lead to ultimate blockage inside the heat exchanger"}, {"pat_id": "US-5776333-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "also, the air-cooler 25 will ensure that incoming raw water cannot be heated within the heat exchanger 18 to a temperature which would induce premature precipitation of dissolved solids in the incoming raw water, and thus lead to ultimate blockage inside the heat exchanger 18"}, {"pat_id": "US-5858248-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "also, the air-cooler 25 will ensure that incoming raw water cannot be heated within the heat exchanger 18 to a temperature which would induce premature precipitation of dissolved solids in the incoming raw water, and thus lead to ultimate blockage inside the heat exchanger"}, {"pat_id": "US-5562834-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the vaporized organic contaminants and steam removed from the top of the steam stripper are passed through a heat exchanger to raise the temperature of the stream to about 400 c"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102082802-B1", "para_id": "claim_3", "text": "and (1) when the controller 200 determines that the sum of the influence value a2 due to the water temperature and the influence value a4 due to the membrane contamination is greater than the preset limit value, the water treatment system using a heat exchanger"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0373577-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "because of the lower temperature level of the incoming water vapor-containing flue gas, high-temperature corrosion can be avoided in the heat exchanger (13) and even a heated heat transfer medium with a higher temperature than in line (12) of fig"}, {"pat_id": "JP-6593422-B2", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "a method of inhibiting corrosion, at least a part of the cooling target device group is subjected to indirect cooling via a heat exchanger between the cooling water passing through the steel pipe and the cooling target device, and the temperature of the cooling water after heat exchange becomes high"}, {"pat_id": "US-9810377-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "this heat exchanger interface will help in keeping the temperature of the fluid in the modified inlet block 444 constant during the pressure decay, thereby improving the accuracy of the rate-of-decay measurement by avoiding fluctuations in the rate that may have otherwise been cause by fluctuations in the temperature of the modified inlet block 444"}, {"pat_id": "US-6562205-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the exchanger 24 is therefore a heat exchanger of titanium from which metal ions are almost unlikely to dissolve out so as to prevent degradation of the high-temperature ultrapure water eventually obtained"}, {"pat_id": "EP-1218293-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "this ensures that the outgoing treated water 19 no longer has a temperature which can cause bicarbonate decomposition and solid deposition within the heat exchanger 18"}, {"pat_id": "EP-1228003-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "this ensures that the outgoing treated water 19 no longer has a temperature which can cause bicarbonate decomposition and solid deposition within the heat exchanger 18"}, {"pat_id": "US-5776333-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this ensures that the outgoing treated water 19 no longer has a temperature which can cause bicarbonate decomposition and solid deposition within the heat exchanger 18"}, {"pat_id": "US-5858248-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this ensures that the outgoing treated water 19 no longer has a temperature which can cause bicarbonate decomposition and solid deposition within the heat exchanger 18"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200454214-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a heat exchanger provided with a coil or plate type softening line to increase the temperature of soft water by heat exchange between soft water supplied from a softener and sodium hypochlorite flowing from the electrolysis tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200454214-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a heat exchanger provided with a coil or plate type softening line to increase the temperature of soft water by heat exchange between soft water supplied from a softener and sodium hypochlorite flowing from the electrolysis tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102082802-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "and (l1) when the controller 200 determines that the sum of the influence value a2 due to the water temperature and the influence value a4 due to the membrane fouling is greater than the preset limit value, the water treatment using a heat exchanger"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102082802-B1", "para_id": "para_32", "text": "in this case, the controller 200 determines that the sum of the influence value a2 due to the water temperature and the influence value a4 due to the membrane fouling exceeds a preset limit value, and the control method of the present invention is applied using a heat exchanger"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0008176-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "since the water is drawn off at the water temperature prevailing in the receptacle, the addition of that water to the flow through the heat exchanger in which the waste water gives off heat does not result in any cooling of this flow with the above- mentioned concomitant disadvantages and risks of freezing in the heat exchanger"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in the illustrated embodiment of the tank water heater 10 and the alternative embodiment of the tankless water heater, if the temperature of condensate is equal to or close to the temperature of room air, the controller 142 determines at box 245 that there is no leakage of water (from the tank 14, or from the heat exchanger coil in the alternative embodiment)"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in the illustrated embodiment of the tank water heater 10 and the alternative embodiment of the tankless water heater, if the temperature of condensate is equal to or close to the temperature of room air, the controller 142 determines at box 245 that there is no leakage of water (from the tank 14, or from the heat exchanger coil in the alternative embodiment)"}, {"pat_id": "US-6121179-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus the input stream may preferably be heated to above the oxidation reaction ignition temperature without substantial heat exchange with an external source of heat--that is, without substantial heat exchange with other fluids via a heat exchanger, fired heater, or the like"}, {"pat_id": "EP-1565408-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "after the lower layer 23 has thus been heated to the desired temperature, the pump 7 can be activated for pumping water from the pit 4 through the heat exchanger to the evaporator"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0354914-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "installations of water-air heat exchangers of different kinds, heat batteries in air conditioning equipment, ordinary water radiators etc often have problems with pipe ruptures due to freezing in low air temperatures"}, {"pat_id": "US-7909895-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "while passing through the heat exchanger 113, the slurry is further heated to the desired temperature at which the biosolids cell walls will rupture and to liberate water bound in the cells"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101758303-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "[ it can be seen that the temperature of the treated effluent discharged from the heat exchanger is maintained below a certain maximum temperature (e.g., about 45 c) to prevent scaling"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200454214-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a heat exchanger provided with a coil or plate type softening line to increase the temperature of soft water by heat exchange between soft water supplied from a softener and sodium hypochlorite flowing from the electrolysis tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200454214-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a heat exchanger provided with a coil or plate type softening line to increase the temperature of soft water by heat exchange between soft water supplied from a softener and sodium hypochlorite flowing from the electrolysis tank"}, {"pat_id": "EP-1218293-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "the purpose of the intercooler 118 is to cool the treated water to a temperature sufficiently low so as not to cause hardness in the untreated water passing through the heat exchanger to precipitate and form scale in the heat exchange cartridge 116 and the conduits feeding the untreated water from the heat exchange cartridge 116 to the water treatment cartridge 114"}, {"pat_id": "EP-1228003-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "the purpose of the intercooler 118 is to cool the treated water to a temperature sufficiently low so as not to cause hardness in the untreated water passing through the heat exchanger to precipitate and form scale in the heat exchange cartridge 116 and the conduits feeding the untreated water from the heat exchange cartridge 116 to the water treatment cartridge 114"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102081866-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in order to avoid the use of expensive sensors necessary to withstand the temperature rise of the evaporator /