roduce at least one fine stream that allows at least some of the water to evaporate while in the air, which leaves the salt to fall into the collection pit 162"}, {"pat_id": "US-9005310-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the nozzle may be configured to produce at least one fine stream that allows at least some of the water to evaporate while in the air, which leaves the salt to fall into the collection pit 162"}, {"pat_id": "US-8312930-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the fluid stream exiting from discharge nozzle 36 is at such a high pressure that the stream can extend through the perforations to break up pluggage also found incrusting the gravel pack"}, {"pat_id": "US-10926284-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the collector(s) may be configured to receive a volume of water projected at least the horizontal distance from the nozzles, e.g., the water jet/stream from the nozzle should generally traverse at least the distance of displacement between the nozzle and the collector, to the extent it is aimed to reduce water loss"}]</data>
