  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-11112190-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "at block 1806, the method includes affecting the temperature of the transported fluid in the pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-11112190-B2", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the promoting of heat transfer (block 1804) from the environment to the pipeline (e.g., when the external temperature is above a threshold) may increase the temperature of the fluid in the pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "US-11193847-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, in such embodiments, based on the sensor data determined by the temperature sensors 52, the control sub-system 54 may determine fluid temperature at multiple different locations along the bore in the pipeline system 10 (process block 106)"}, {"pat_id": "US-11199502-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is very easy to produce the natural gas hydrate in the oil and gas exploitation and transportation process especially in low-temperature and high-pressure deep water environments, and the natural gas hydrate will block a conveying pipeline"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101454539-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "first, the offshore plant 100 according to the prior art resumes the operation of transferring marine resources, and as the temperature of the marine resources is rapidly lowered due to the row thompson effect, the pipeline 130 is damaged due to temperature drop there is a problem that there is a risk of breakage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101454539-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "summary of the invention the present invention has been made to solve the above problems and it is an object of the present invention to provide a multiple pressure regulator for an offshore plant which can reduce the risk of damage or breakage of a pipeline due to a rapid temperature drop in the process of transferring marine resources"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101454539-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "accordingly, the multiple pressure regulating device 1 for an offshore plant according to the present invention can reduce the risk of damage or breakage of the pipeline 40 due to a temperature drop, the effect of increasing the durability of the line 40 can be obtained"}, {"pat_id": "US-8117998-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is possible to prevent pipelines from freezing and bursting at temperatures below zero during the winter, using the configuration of the hot water supplying system 20"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "after turning on the pump and allowing the hot water to flow through the first set of pipelines in the first loop on the property for the period of time, checking a temperature of all floors of the property to determine if there is a noticeable increase in temperature of a particular floor anywhere on the property"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "after turning on the recirculation pump and allowing the hot water to flow through the first set of pipelines in the first loop on the property for the period of time, checking a temperature of all floors of the property to determine if there is a noticeable increase in temperature of a particular floor anywhere on the property"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after turning on the pump and allowing the hot water to flow through the first set of pipelines in the first loop on the property for the period of time, the method may include checking a temperature of all floors of the property to determine if there is a noticeable increase in temperature of a particular floor anywhere on the property"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "after turning on the recirculation pump and allowing the hot water to flow through the first set of pipelines in the first loop on the property for the period of time, checking a temperature of all floors of the property to determine if there is a noticeable increase in temperature of a particular floor anywhere on the property"}, {"pat_id": "US-12442540-B1", "para_i