  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, the water supply control device 250 by checking the pressure in the water supply pipe 230 through the pressure sensor unit 260, it is possible to prevent the water from flowing into the water supply pipe 230 is frozen or blocked due to low temperature, the pipe is broken"}, {"pat_id": "US-11066813-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in some example embodiments, the temperature sensor (115) may be used to prevent pipes from freezing, and the pressure sensor (115) may be used to prevent pipes from bursting"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, the water supply control device 250 by checking the pressure in the water supply pipe 230 through the pressure sensor unit 260, it is possible to prevent the water from flowing into the water supply pipe 230 is frozen or blocked due to low temperature, the pipe is broken"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3706066-B1", "para_id": "para_16", "text": "in another embodiment, not covered by the claimed invention, moreover the pressure sensor comprises another bragg grating, installed on a part of said sensor not deforming after pressure, such for example a cylindrical body, so that it is subject only to deformation due to temperature"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3706066-B1", "para_id": "para_18", "text": "preferably, in addition the pressure sensor comprises another bragg grating, installed on a part of said sensor not deforming after liquid flow, so that it is subject only to deformation due to temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-11047115-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it should be appreciated that if water temperatures are detected as being close to or below freezing, a pressure sensor may look for an increase in pipe pressure that may indicate freezing water in the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101406507-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, although the present invention is equipped with a pressure sensor for detecting a hydraulic pressure drop occurring when a water pipe leaks, and an acoustic sensor for detecting a sound wave generated when a water pipe leaks, a compact arrangement is possible, and a sound / pressure composite sensor which prevents excessive increase of the temperature of the leaked water"}, {"pat_id": "US-11549837-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "thus, a single set of localized sensors (flow rate sensor 105, optional pressure sensor 65, optional acoustic sensor, and/or optional temperature sensor 93) can be utilized and incorporated into the water meter and leak detection system 10 (126 shown in figs"}, {"pat_id": "US-11549837-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "thus, a single set of localized sensors (flow rate sensor 105, optional pressure sensor 65, optional acoustic sensor, and/or optional temperature sensor 93) can be utilized and incorporated into the water meter and leak detection system 10 (126 shown in figs"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102081866-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in order to avoid the use of expensive sensors necessary to withstand the temperature rise of the evaporator / condenser 4002, pressure sensors p e and p c correspond to the low temperature side of the heat exchanger 4004 and control valves v e and v c ) can be mounted on the fluid line"}]</data>
