  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-200475713-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the rainwater in the block is usually removed by using a pneumatic pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200475713-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "most of the rainwater is removed through the siphon principle, and only the remaining rainwater is removed by the pneumatic pump in removing the rainwater accumulated in the hull block, etc., so that the rainwater can be quickly removed and the air consumption can be minimized"}, {"pat_id": "JP-7774358-B1", "para_id": "para_54", "text": "when the water level becomes abnormal (rising), factors such as blockage of the discharge pipe, backflow from the discharge pipe (rainwater, etc.), failure of the discharge pump, or blockage of the return pipe 25 cause the water level to rise from the normal water level, causing the floating body 1 to tilt more"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100823240-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, when the initial rainwater and sediment contaminants are completely excluded from the initial rainwater treatment facility 1 and the pressure or water level becomes zero, the drain pump 21 receiving the water is driven to operate the water tank 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100895623-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the submersible pump according to an embodiment of the present invention can take in the upper rainwater of the rainwater through the intake port instead of inhaling the water near the bottom like the conventional submersible pump, it is effective to prevent contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101053877-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the submersible pump according to an embodiment of the present invention can take in the upper rainwater of the rainwater through the intake port instead of inhaling the water near the bottom like the conventional submersible pump, it is effective to prevent contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "of the pump (700), thereby forming a flow for preventing decay of the water stored in the rainwater storage tank (200)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "7) in addition, in order to form a flow to prevent the decay of water stored in the rainwater storage tank (200), a bypass pipe (620) may be installed on the opposite edge of the suction pipe (710) to supply water into the interior of the rainwater storage tank (200) by a pump (700)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "the structure of the suction pipe (710) or bypass pipe (620) of the pump (700) forms a flow to prevent the decay of water stored in the rainwater storage tank (200) separately from the agitating unit (500)"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0535375-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "due to the use of the pump, the rainwater channel and the dirty water channel 4 can be at any level to each other, i.e"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101246202-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the water collecting groove 402 provides a volume for collecting water introduced into the concrete structure 400 due to leakage of water supply pipes or inflow of rainwater, and a worker is provided with a water pump (hereinafter, not shown) separately provided through the inspection opening 401"}, {"pat_id": "JP-2663214-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the first rainwater retaining pipe 5 is parallel to the sewer pipe 1 up to the location corresponding to the underground water diversion chamber 2, the portion from the top of the drainage pit 14 at the lower end of the pit 13 for pumping water gradually descends downward from the sewer line 1 while tilting"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200324955-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when it rains, the sewage is treated in the same way as above, and the rainwater that is exceeding the sewage treatment amount (exactly diluted sewage mixed with rainwater) is pumped by the rainwater transfer pump (bar), and the rainwater distribution tank (3) next, the supernatant is precipitated in the storm sedimentation basin (5)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200295999-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the purpose is to prevent the failure and wear of the submersible pump 60 due to frequent starting and stopping of the submersible pump 60 for use of rainwater in toilet water or landscape water, thereby prolonging its life"}]</data>
