e water tank 10"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5042805-B2", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "specifically, when the water level gauge 111 detects that the water level in the contaminant removal tank 110 is higher than the specified water level, control is performed to relatively increase the amount of water transferred by the advection pump 122, and the contamination level is also increased"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101113083-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in addition, the pump well 46 operates the transfer pump when a certain water level is reached while storing the treated water discharged from the organic material decay reaction tank 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101113090-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the pump well 46 is provided with a transfer pump that operates when the predetermined water level is reached while storing the treated water discharged from the organic material decay reaction tank 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101113090-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in addition, the pump well 46 operates the transfer pump when a certain water level is reached while storing the treated water discharged from the organic material decay reaction tank 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100720388-B1", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "in accordance with the set water level value of the second water level detection unit 140 to operate the circulation pump 150a, while continuously operating the primary electrolysis cell 130a so that the circulating sterilizing material is repeatedly electrolyzed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100720388-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in accordance with the set water level value of the second water level detection unit 140 to operate the circulation pump 150a, while continuously operating the primary electrolysis cell 130a so that the circulating sterilizing material is repeatedly electrolyzed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101427989-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, at the detection level of the first water level sensor (w / l 1), the first pump (p1) operates until the i