  <data key="d5">["self", "road", "rain", "contaminant", "sub", "preventing", "rainfall", "pressure", "filter", "earthworm", "joint", "prevention", "body", "construction", "smell", "fume", "ground", "shield", "structure", "force", "operation", "maintenance", "door", "deformation", "passage", "object", "sewer", "connection", "sidewalk", "hole", "outlet", "filtration", "surface", "leakage", "mortar", "malodor", "sewage", "treatment", "increase", "stability", "sinkhole", "order", "inlet", "tank", "part", "water", "area", "drain", "spring", "earth", "portion", "apparatus", "harbor", "function", "windwater", "weight", "like", "pipe", "problem", "storm", "filling", "embodiment", "collector", "level", "rainwater", "sinking", "odor", "receiver", "housing", "drainage", "discharge", "device", "port", "shielding", "side", "end", "difficulty", "welding", "ability", "enclosure", "damper", "infiltration", "plurality", "leak", "cover", "plate", "inflow", "advantage", "edge", "invention", "opening"]</data>
  <data key="d6">["close", "construct", "have", "provide", "complete", "act", "finish", "block", "discharge", "incline", "contain", "allow", "accord", "catch", "attain", "occur", "join", "match", "perform", "open", "increase", "connect", "prevent", "form", "cause", "receive", "remove", "flow", "shield", "intercept", "store", "weaken", "cover", "equip", "insert", "relate", "adsorb", "shut off", "be", "describe", "push", "transfer", "treat", "comprise", "ensure", "include", "instal"]</data>
  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-200167095-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the sewage receiver was installed when the hydraulic pressure acted to block the odor, and when the hydraulic pressure was removed, there was a damper of a structure that automatically shuts off the drain by self-weight or spring force"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200361466-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "bad smell intercepting apparatus of rain and dirty water receiver the present invention relates to a malodor blocking device of a rainwater receiver, and more particularly, to increase the water level and to increase the water level at the discharge end of the openable malodor blocking device such that the water pressure pushes the opening door"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200361466-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "to increase the open and close the door smoothly, and even if the water flows little by little to provide a odor blocking device of the rainwater receiver to open and close the door smoothly by the water pressure in the inclined portion of the discharge end"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100750645-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "these storm receivers store the road drainage during rainfall and transfer it to the filtration apparatus to adsorb and remove contaminants contained in the road drainage, and then discharge only the treated water to the sewer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200357071-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "road drainage with first flush treatment ability the present invention is to insert a filter filling tank having a filtration treatment function in the conventional rainwater receiver to the road surface drainage treatment device having an initial excellent treatment function that can reliably remove and treat contaminants contained in the road surface drainage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100975670-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by allowing the infiltration water of the ground to flow into the lower part of the rain receiver body 10 by the inflow drain hole 14, it is possible to prevent deformation due to an increase in the earth pressure acting on the rain receiver body 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200361466-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "bad smell intercepting apparatus of rain and dirty water receiver the present invention relates to a malodor blocking device of a rainwater receiver, and more particularly, to increase the water level and to increase the water level at the discharge end of the openable malodor blocking device such that the water pressure pushes the opening door"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101715262-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, there has recently been a problem in that leaks occur in the rainwater harbor connection port to weaken the ground where the rainwater receiver is installed, and furthermore, there is a problem that the sinkhole is formed due to the leakage of the earthworm"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101715262-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thirdly, there is an advantage that the sinking of the ground caused by the rainwater receiver can be prevented by leakage of the rainwater due to the mortar operation finishing of the joint between the rainwater collector and the connecting pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200322595-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "there is considerable difficulty in construction because the inlet pipe connection part or outlet pipe connection part of the receiver does not match, and if the inlet pipe or outlet pipe which is already constructed is forcibly bent and connected to the rainwater receiver, the connection part is weak and easily leaks"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101167604-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "since the connection pipe p1 can be inclined, the drain port 115 provided in the rainwater receiver can be conveniently connected to the connection fume pipe (drain pipe), thereby preventing leakage at the connection portion"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632920-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is another object of the present invention to provide a malodor leakage prevention device capable of smoothly performing an excellent discharge operation and an odor shielding function by ensuring stability of operation and a rainwater receiver equipped with the same"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632920-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in order to attain the above object, the malodor leakage prevention device according to the present invention is a malodor leakage prevention device installed in a rainwater receiver, comprising"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632920-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in order to attain the above object, the malodor leakage prevention device according to the present invention is a malodor leakage prevention device installed in a rainwater receiver, comprising"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632920-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in order to attain the above object, the malodor leakage prevention device according to the present invention is a malodor leakage prevention device installed in a rainwater receiver, comprising"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632920-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and a malodor leakage prevention device installed inside the rainwater receiver housing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632920-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "meanwhile, the malodor leakage prevention device (v) according to the present invention can be constructed by directly installing the shield plate (2) having the above-described structure on the rainwater receiver housing, and a sub housing (1)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632920-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "5a and 5b, the rainwater collector having the malodor leakage prevention device includes a rainwater receiver enclosure 6 having a drainage passage formed therein, and a plurality of fine inflow holes formed on the rainwater receiver enclosure 6 a rainwater catching cover 7, and a malodor leakage preventing device v installed in the rainwater catching enclosure 6"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632920-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "hereinafter, the malodor leakage prevention device according to the first embodiment of the present invention and the operation of the rainwater receiver having the same will be briefly described"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632920-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thereafter, the odor leakage preventing device (v) is joined to the lower housing part (62) of the rainwater receiver by welding or the like to complete the rainwater receiver, and then the windwater is installed at the edge of the road or the sidewalk, the cover 7 is installed"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101715262-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, there has recently been a problem in that leaks occur in the rainwater harbor connection port to weaken the ground where the rainwater receiver is installed, and furthermore, there is a problem that the sinkhole is formed due to the leakage of the earthworm"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101715262-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thirdly, there is an advantage that the sinking of the ground caused by the rainwater receiver can be prevented by leakage of the rainwater due to the mortar operation finishing of the joint between the rainwater collector and the connecting pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101632920-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is another object of the present invention to provide a malodor leakage prevention device capable of smoothly performing an excellent discharge operation and an odor shielding function by ensuring stability of operation and a rainwater receiver equipped with the same"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and an auxiliary shielding plate installed at an upper side of the rain receiver, the maintenance tank, and the treatment tank to cover an area of the whole thereof, and having an auxiliary shield plate for shielding the upper opening of the treatment tank on one side of the bottom surface, and receiving the road surface drainage"}]</data>
</edge>
