  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101485001-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a stormwater receiver (100) a permeable sidewalk block (200) constituting the sidewalk and configured to allow the storm to penetrate into the bedrock"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101485001-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, the rainwater infiltrated through the permeable press block flows directly into the reservoir 500 through the induction pipe installed under the permeable press block, and the road effluent flowing through the rainwater receiver on the road passes through the filtration tank and then flows into the storage tank 500 after the initial storm has been processed through the storage tank 300"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "(7) the maintenance and treatment tanks can be installed in a block block made of concrete, or forcedly installed together with the storm water receiver"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100750645-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "these storm receivers store the road drainage during rainfall and transfer it to the filtration apparatus to adsorb and remove contaminants contained in the road drainage, and then discharge only the treated water to the sewer"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100975670-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, it is possible to prevent the deformation caused by the rise of the earth pressure acting on the storm receiver body by allowing the surface infiltration water flows into the lower portion of the storm receiver body"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as a result, deposits absorbing contaminants are deposited in the mud at the bottom of the storm receiver 20, the maintenance tank 30, and the treatment tank 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, if the removal process of the contaminants continues, the bottom of the storm receiver 20, the maintenance tank 30 and the treatment tank 40, deposits containing contaminants are deposited, and the filter medium filling tank ( 70) contaminants will also collect inside, and regular removal will be required"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101280771-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the storm flows into the inlet chamber 123a3 and the contaminants are removed by the obstacle receiver 123b during the passage through the inlet chamber 123a3"}]</data>
</edge>
