  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-12231085-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the moisture collection layer 40 may additionally and/or alternatively prevent the energy dissipating receiver 20 from cracking and/or freezing, such as during circumstances when there are large temperature changes"}, {"pat_id": "US-12231085-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "rather than both reducing a temperature of the energy dissipating receiver to reduce degradation of the energy dissipating receiver 20 and produce water, the water producing system 100 may produce and/or collect water"}, {"pat_id": "US-12231085-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the moisture collection layer 40 may additionally and/or alternatively prevent the energy dissipating receiver 20 from cracking and/or freezing, such as during circumstances when there are large temperature changes"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101408121-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the plurality of detection sensors may be different depending on the structure or form of the cold / hot water supply device 100, and may include, for example, a water level sensor 612, cold water (hot water) temperature sensors 624 and 634, (wire or the like) sensor signal receiver 740 receives signals from the plurality of sensor sensors 640, 660, a water leakage sensor 670, one or more overflow sensors 690, can do"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101408121-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the plurality of detection sensors may be different depending on the structure or form of the cold / hot water supply device 100, and may include, for example, a water level sensor 612, cold water (hot water) temperature sensors 624 and 634, (wire or the like) sensor signal receiver 740 receives signals from the plurality of sensor sensors 640, 660, a water leakage sensor 670, one or more overflow sensors 690, can do"}, {"pat_id": "US-7951298-B2", "para_id": "claim_20", "text": "a receiver in communication with one or more oxidation-reduction potential ( orp ) probes, a subset of the probes being activated, each activated orp probe operable to measure a real-time orp in situ and at operating temperature and pressure for one or more of the phases, and one or more of the selected zones including at least one orp probe"}]</data>
</edge>
