  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101196227-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, in order to prepare for the water shortage situation, there are ways to minimize the problems of securing the water by blocking the above-mentioned large artificial dam, reservoir or river water, and to secure the water that is insufficient without performing relatively large construction"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101518747-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the shore protection block of the present invention can be installed in a lake, a dam reservoir slope, a river, or a ditch to provide a space where various aquatic plants, aquatic insects and fish can coexist along with water purification.10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101048805-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "as described above, the characteristics of the present invention is in the partition wall, the purpose of installing the partition wall is to induce the flow of water fines or contaminants contained in the river water this prevents sedimentation so that no blockage occurs at the bottom of the reservoir"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100748018-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, if the water stays in the reservoir for a long time, the contaminants are increased by condensation and contaminate the river water rather than being decomposed naturally"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100748018-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, if the water is confined to a certain place for a long time, the pollution is aggravated by the agglomeration of substances, so that the water stored in the reservoir can be discharged from the water through the gate and refilled with new water to prevent the contamination of the river water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100906654-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "unlike rivers that flow naturally by gravity, reservoirs or lakes are characterized by the accumulation of contaminants in lakes in the event of large or prolonged contamination (in most cases)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101067632-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "of the reservoir or river prevents turbid water diffusion that prevents contamination of the reservoir or stream so that it is economically appropriately blocked before it spreads inward, so that only clean water from which the soil and contaminants have been removed from the turbid water flows into the reservoir or stream to prevent contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101199427-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the present invention relates to a purification system for dredged soil which can prevent secondary pollution by purifying dirty water in a clean state and re-injecting it into a river or reservoir"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101006852-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "here, since the partitions 12 and 13 do not receive great force only to induce the flow of the river water, it is important to install the thin walls so as not to reduce the area of the reservoir 11 while the river water does not leak"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101429033-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "while the mobile water purification apparatus 200 is moving in a reservoir or a river, the obstacle detection sensor outputs obstacle detection information to the automatic control unit 280 when it detects an obstacle"}, {"pat_id": "US-8074670-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this tendency is only amplified due to the fact that porosity reservoirs are typically constructed within the alluvial soils of a river bed so that there is an upstream and downstream portion to the reservoir corresponding to the overall valley gradient"}, {"pat_id": "US-8074670-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "due to a natural gradient of the land where porosity reservoir is formed (e.g., along a river bed), the reservoir defines an upstream end and a downstream end"}]</data>
