  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101583008-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "1, the bimetal 23 or 23 the heater power is directly applied to the steam generating part 20 and the power is not applied to the bimetal 23 or 23 so that the bimetal 23 or 23 can not function as a temperature sensor, accordingly, the bimetal 23 or 23 can not block the input of the heater power when the steam generating part 20 overheats, and thus the steam thawing device can not be operated safely"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200383900-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "and a cpu that controls a current controller to block a current flowing through the electrode plate when the temperature of the inflow water detected by the temperature sensor is equal to or greater than a predetermined reference temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-10948131-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "moreover, in some embodiments, the control sub-system 50 may determine fluid temperature within the tubing annulus 25 of the pipe segment 20 based on sensor data determined by a fluid temperature annulus sensor 54 (process block 118)"}, {"pat_id": "US-11193847-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, in such embodiments, based on the sensor data determined by the temperature sensors 52, the control sub-system 54 may determine fluid temperature at multiple different locations along the bore in the pipeline system 10 (process block 106)"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "if, at block 7069, the system 6000 is currently in a normal water production mode, the target temperature 7068 along with a product or condensate output temperature 7070 determined from data provided by a product output sensor (e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "in some embodiments, the individual derivatives determined from each product temperature sensor 6082a-d may all be required to be less than the threshold in order for the controller 6034 to proceed to block 7840"}, {"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "in some embodiments, if any of the individual derivatives determined from each product temperature sensor 6082a-d are less than the threshold, the controller 6034 may proceed to block 7844"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "if, at block 7069, the system 6000 is currently in a normal water production mode, the target temperature 7068 along with a product or condensate output temperature 7070 determined from data provided by a product output sensor (e.g"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in some embodiments, the individual derivatives determined from each product temperature sensor 6082a-d may all be required to be less than the threshold in order for the controller 6034 to proceed to block 7840"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in some embodiments, if any of the individual derivatives determined from each product temperature sensor 6082a-d are less than the threshold, the controller 6034 may proceed to block 7844"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "claim_8", "text": "optionally wherein the drain blockage is determined by the controller (142) when the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor (414) is about the same as the temperature reading of the second temperature sensor (418)"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the controller 142 is further configured to compare the temperature readings of the first, second, and third temperature sensors 114, 118, 122 to determine whether an error has occurred in the water heater 10 (e.g., leakage, drain blockage), as further discussed below"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "alternatively, the temperature readings of the first temperature sensor 414 during the heating mode may also be used to determine a drain blockage"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in particular, when the temperature readings of the first temperature sensor 414 decrease toward the minimum temperature limit 682 during the heating mode, the controller will determine that there is a drain blockage"}, {"pat_id": "US-11761838-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "when the temperature distribution in equipment such as pumps, rotors, compressors and turbines changes or when the temperature ranges exceed normal values, the nanoparticles based sensors can alert and prevent breakage and down time of the asset"}, {"pat_id": "US-11066813-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in some example embodiments, the temperature sensor (115) may be used to prevent pipes from freezing, and the pressure sensor (115) may be used to prevent pipes from bursting"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, the water supply control device 250 by checking the pressure in the water supply pipe 230 through the pressure sensor unit 260, it is possible to prevent the water from flowing into the water supply pipe 230 is frozen or blocked due to low temperature, the pipe is broken"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101327389-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, by checking the condensate and curing temperature throughout the construction by the moisture sensor and the temperature sensor, it is possible to contribute to the quality improvement by checking the uniform curing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101147332-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "water pollution monitoring system according to the prior art, by providing a temperature control device inside the water pollution monitoring system so that the sensitivity of the sensor is not affected by the external temperature, and also provides a sensor cleaning device inside the sensor to improve the sensitivity of the sensor it s about making sure you re not affected by contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "US-11892393-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for example, as noted above, the rate of deposit of lead oxide on the contaminant sensor 175 is dependent on ph, temperature, conductivity, and ionic strength"}, {"pat_id": "US-6315886-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the invention contemplates in-line monitoring with sensors and microprocessors for automatic computer-assisted process control, such as ph sensors, uv and visible light, sensors for biological contaminants, temperature, etc"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3032245-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the impedance of the circulating liquid and the surface of the detection electrode 1 measured by the anticorrosion performance degradation detection sensor 10 increases by 2% when the temperature of the circulating liquid decreases by 1 c"}, {"pat_id": "US-10722824-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in second (sensor) compartment 23 to determine the temperature at the ph and corrosion sensors and permit correction of their readings"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101521944-B1", "para_id": "claim_12", "text": "a heating control method for a steam cracking device, a step of applying a heater power to the steam heating element when the steam generating switch is turned on while the power switch is turned on and measuring the temperature of the steam heating element through the steam heating element temperature sensor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101967405-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "therefore, if a point sensor is used to measure the temperature and strain in the water pipe, it is not possible to confirm the position of the sensor even if leakage or deformation occurs in the interval between the sensors"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3032245-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "the impedance of the circulating liquid and the surface of the detection electrode 1 measured by the anticorrosion performance degradation detection sensor 10 increases by 2% when the temperature of the circulating liquid decreases by 1 c"}, {"pat_id": "US-11892393-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "for example, as noted above, the rate of deposit of lead oxide on the contaminant sensor 175 is dependent on ph, temperature, conductivity, and ionic strength"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101262046-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "various sensors such as temperature can be installed to detect the change of concentration of sterilization ion efficiently and actively.in order to efficiently generate concentration of sterilization ion through electrolysis when water passes, the electrode affects the flow rate of water"}, {"pat_id": "US-10753900-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "because the resistance of meas can directly demonstrate the electrode fouling status, the resistance of each mea sensors was used as an indicator of the whole mea and measured at ambient temperature (25 c.) using a digital multimeter weekly for 4 weeks to elucidate the electrode fouling influence"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3769176-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "temperature sensor 38 is used to collect real-time temperature data and monitor the temperature of the incoming water to determine if conditions are conducive to pipe freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100634761-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when it is determined that the communication state is good, the temperature data of the water tank together with the ambient temperature data (which can determine the possibility of freezing of the water pipe, measured by the temperature sensor) and (if the pump abnormality can be determined) preferably, a current sensor is further provided to control the pump using the current data supplied to the pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "according to this aspect of the present invention, the water supply control device checks the outside air temperature sensed by the temperature sensor and intermittently drives the pump to prevent freezing of the water supply pipe supplying water to the water tank of the drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the outside air temperature falls below the reference value through the temperature sensor 270, the water supply control device 200 intermittently drives the pump 220 to prevent freezing of the water supply pipe 230"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100991888-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, the controller c opens the first opening / closing valve v\u2081 and simultaneously shuts off the second opening / closing valve v2 when the temperature sensor 13 detects the expected temperature of the freezing wave"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101289929-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the controller 14 may be provided with information on the temperature of the water in the water pipe detected by the temperature detection sensor 12, and determine the freezing time of the water in the water pipe by grasping the temperature change of the water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101541137-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "3, when the temperature of the ballast water w sensed by the sensor unit 300 becomes higher than the freezing point of the preset ballast water w, the control unit 500 outputs a drive stop signal can be applied"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101942221-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the purging control unit 47 operates the freezing unit 43 and the heating unit 45 on the basis of the temperature information transmitted through the first sensor unit 33 and the second sensor unit 35 determine how many degrees the cooling or heating temperature should be adjusted"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101961095-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by the temperature sensor and the power is supplied to the power storage unit 20, thereby preventing freezing of the main body 1 and the tube 70"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102193417-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the control unit determines whether or not a heating wire that is mounted inside the lower frame of the main body and prevents freezing of the side channel using the temperature measurement value and the humidity measurement value measured by the temperature sensor and the humidity sensor is driven"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102193417-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the step of determining whether the heating wire is driven by the control unit (s200), the control unit of the freezing prevention system determines whether the heating wire 300 is driven using a temperature measurement value, a humidity measurement value measured by a temperature sensor, a humidity sensor, etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102193417-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "here, the temperature measurement value and the humidity measurement value transmitted through the data connection line 510 from the temperature sensor and the humidity sensor are compared with the temperature threshold value and the humidity threshold value, respectively, and the temperature measurement value is less than the temperature threshold value, and the humidity measurement value if it is determined that there is a risk of freezing or freezing above this humidity threshold, it is determined to drive the heating wire"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102332096-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "in this way, when the hot air blower is driven (by driving the heater 20 and the fan 30) to generate and blow hot air, the indoor temperature is measured through the temperature sensor 10, and the measured indoor temperature is above the freezing prevention safety temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102498793-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "in the heating element 40, the temperature sensor 64 installed in the water supply pipe detects the temperature of the water supply pipe, transmits the detected information to the controller box 60, and the controller box analyzes the detected information to determine the prediction of freezing and bursting"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200310444-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the present invention, by simply installing the device around the water pipe and connecting only the power supply, the sensor detects that the temperature drops to sub-zero temperatures and heats the heating sheet to prevent freezing phenomenon that the water pipe freezes or freezes in winter"}, {"pat_id": "US-11047115-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it should be appreciated that if water temperatures are detected as being close to or below freezing, a pressure sensor may look for an increase in pipe pressure that may indicate freezing water in the pipe"}, {"pat_id": "US-6021798-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the temperature rises above freezing, the sensor is de-actuated to interrupt the flow of electricity from the power source to the solenoid-actuated valve, and thereby close the valve and stop the flow of water therethrough"}, {"pat_id": "US-6436299-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the ambient temperature sensor circuit measures the ambient temperature of the atmosphere, so that the water treatment system can maintain a temperature level above freezing or some other predetermined temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-6436299-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the ambient temperature sensor circuit 114 measures the ambient temperature of the atmosphere so that the water treatment system 10 can maintain a temperature level above freezing or some other predetermined temperature setting"}, {"pat_id": "US-4922233-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "monitoring systems presently used to monitor the condition of a drain valve and employing differential temperature sensors are ineffective or insufficient for a number of reasons"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the controller 142 is further configured to compare the temperature readings of the first, second, and third temperature sensors 114, 118, 122 to determine whether an error has occurred in the water heater 10 (e.g., leakage, drain blockage), as further discussed below"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "for example, should the controller determine that the tolerance has changed from 0.5 c to 1.5 c (one f to three f) between the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 114 and the third temperature sensor 122 during the standby mode, the controller may determine there is a leakage and indicate to a user to check the water heater"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "rather, only differences between the exhaust assembly 30 and the exhaust assembly 330 are specifically noted herein, such as differences in the positioning of the temperature sensors, and how the control system determines a leakage"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "10, the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 will increase (i.e., positive rate of change) again to a second peak or leakage temperature limit 690a after the water heater enters the standby mode from the heating mode"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in particular, the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 will increase to the leakage temperature limit 690a shortly after (e.g., about two minutes"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the wait period 695 ends when the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 detects a shift or change in state from the negative rate of change to the positive rate of change during the standby mode in which the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 begins to increase toward the leakage temperature limit 690a"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "rather, the first temperature sensor 414 may be detecting a temperature of the residual condensate produced during the heating mode that has already begun to cool to a lower temperature (i.e., temperature lower than the leaking water) within the drain line 394"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the wait period 695 ends when the leaking water has reached a predetermined water level in the drain pipe 394, and the leaking water is then able to exit through the drain line 398 past the first temperature sensor 414"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "9-11, only the first temperature sensor 414 is used to determine a leakage"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "further, since any slight increase in the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 at the end of the wait period 695 might indicate that there is a leak, the controller may be able to detect even smaller leaks"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "9 represents another way that the temperature sensors may be positioned in a condensing water heater and used to determine a leakage in the water heater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101406507-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, although the present invention is equipped with a pressure sensor for detecting a hydraulic pressure drop occurring when a water pipe leaks, and an acoustic sensor for detecting a sound wave generated when a water pipe leaks, a compact arrangement is possible, and a sound / pressure composite sensor which prevents excessive increase of the temperature of the leaked water"}, {"pat_id": "US-11549837-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "thus, a single set of localized sensors (flow rate sensor 105, optional pressure sensor 65, optional acoustic sensor, and/or optional temperature sensor 93) can be utilized and incorporated into the water meter and leak detection system 10 (126 shown in figs"}, {"pat_id": "US-11814821-B2", "para_id": "claim_2", "text": "and a leak detector controller in communication with said first sensor and said second sensor configured to sense said ambient temperature from said first sensor and generating said drive signal to drive said second sensor to said elevated temperature greater than said ambient temperature and to generate a leak signal when said drive signal of said second sensor exceeds a leak point value"}, {"pat_id": "US-11814821-B2", "para_id": "claim_18", "text": "and a leak detector controller in communication with said first sensor and said second sensor configured to sense said ambient temperature from said first sensor and generating said drive signal to drive said second sensor to said elevated temperature greater than said ambient temperature and to generate said leak condition when said drive signal of said second sensor exceeds a leak point value"}, {"pat_id": "US-5638847-A", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "moreover, the moisture and temperature sensors may not be positioned to detect a leak, for incipient freeze condition, and thus, the flow sensor would provide the last line of defense to water damage"}, {"pat_id": "US-7549435-B2", "para_id": "para_51", "text": "in such a configuration, a sensor, such as a temperature sensor, may be included to determine the source of a particular leak among one of a plurality of fluid sources"}, {"pat_id": "US-11549837-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "thus, a single set of localized sensors (flow rate sensor 105, optional pressure sensor 65, optional acoustic sensor, and/or optional temperature sensor 93) can be utilized and incorporated into the water meter and leak detection system 10 (126 shown in figs"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the controller 142 is further configured to compare the temperature readings of the first, second, and third temperature sensors 114, 118, 122 to determine whether an error has occurred in the water heater 10 (e.g., leakage, drain blockage), as further discussed below"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "for example, should the controller determine that the tolerance has changed from 0.5 c to 1.5 c (one f to three f) between the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 114 and the third temperature sensor 122 during the standby mode, the controller may determine there is a leakage and indicate to a user to check the water heater"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "rather, only differences between the exhaust assembly 30 and the exhaust assembly 330 are specifically noted herein, such as differences in the positioning of the temperature sensors, and how the control system determines a leakage"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "10, the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 will increase (i.e., positive rate of change) again to a second peak or leakage temperature limit 690a after the water heater enters the standby mode from the heating mode"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in particular, the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 will increase to the leakage temperature limit 690a shortly after (e.g., about two minutes"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the wait period 695 ends when the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 detects a shift or change in state from the negative rate of change to the positive rate of change during the standby mode in which the temperature reading of the first temperature sensor 414 begins to increase toward the leakage temperature limit 690a"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "9-11, only the first temperature sensor 414 is used to determine a leakage"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "9 represents another way that the temperature sensors may be positioned in a condensing water heater and used to determine a leakage in the water heater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101967405-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "therefore, if a point sensor is used to measure the temperature and strain in the water pipe, it is not possible to confirm the position of the sensor even if leakage or deformation occurs in the interval between the sensors"}, {"pat_id": "US-10537921-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "reference symbol 21 designates a filter unit, reference symbol 23 designates a temperature sensor, reference symbol 25 designates a level sensor, reference symbol 30 designates an object loading unit, reference symbol 31 designates a door lifting drive unit, reference symbol 33 designates a washing lifting drive unit, reference symbol 11 designates spray nozzles, reference symbol 13 designates spray pipelines, reference symbol 15 designates a manual valve, and reference symbol 17 designates electronic valves"}, {"pat_id": "US-12163944-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "typical sensors for monitoring water quality in a spa include in-line sensors, which monitor physical parameters, temperature and flow, and chemical sensors, which monitor conductivity, oxidation reduction potential (orp) and acidity (ph)"}, {"pat_id": "US-11659812-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the sensor 72c may also sense a temperature of the plurality of transmitting coils 721-724 and/or shielding layer 725 and provide a measurement to the power circuit device 715 so that a controller of the printed circuit device 715 may determine whether or not the wireless power transmitter 72 is overheated"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102081866-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in order to avoid the use of expensive sensors necessary to withstand the temperature rise of the evaporator / condenser 4002, pressure sensors p e and p c correspond to the low temperature side of the heat exchanger 4004 and control valves v e and v c ) can be mounted on the fluid line"}]</data>
</edge>
