  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "EP-1226314-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "if conduits draining a large balancing pond or tank of the prior art type become blocked, localised flooding could occur"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101194503-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "figure 7 is a block diagram showing a p-uv sterilization apparatus in the disinfection tank provided in the multifunctional storage system for the initial excellent pollution reduction and urban flooding prevention according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200385155-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in other words, if the raw water flows in excess of the design flow due to natural disasters such as rainy season or flood, natural disasters or unavoidable circumstances, the inflow may not be properly processed and the membrane separation tank overflows and the immersion membrane separator may collapse"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200365446-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by using the control equipment, the water level difference between the upper and the downstream filtration tanks is maintained at 1.0-1.5m, so that the sediment deposited in the upper and the downstream filtration tanks can be gradually discharged during the initial flooding with less floating dust, thereby preventing the ultimate closure of the filter media"}, {"pat_id": "US-4815492-A", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the old type of flood control system known to me to have been used in earlier years is my work utilized a gate valve located outside of a sewer ejector pit or pump tank as contrasted to my prevent invention"}]</data>
