  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-100660052-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "because of this, the block body 30 is installed in a row arrangement of the role of the storage tank for storing rainwater and the waterway line is formed so that the concentrated phenomenon does not occur even in a large amount of rain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101191166-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, since the ground can support the side plate block, the side pressure of the rain water temporarily stored in the storage tank need not be taken into consideration when installing the side plate block"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101248434-B1", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "in this case, between the wall blocks 200 continuously arranged in the transverse direction to form the wall surface of the rainwater storage tank, the engaging portion of the recess portion 210 and the convex portion 220 is formed, and thus the strand wire 10 and the strand wire installation tool ( 100), the fastener 50, etc"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101301345-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, rainwater is circulated through the monthly circulation hole in the storage process, and a large amount of oxygen is supplied into the water, thereby improving water quality by natural purification.1 is a block diagram showing the overall prefabricated rainwater storage tank according to the present invention"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102005372-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, even when the fixed mesh filter 110 is blocked, an appropriate amount of rainwater should be introduced into the float removing tank 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102216793-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, it was configured to block rainwater flowing into the tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102505041-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, the filling pipe 52 is prevented from being clogged by foreign substances remaining in the rainwater flowing into the water collecting channel 41 of the road block 40, so that the filling pipe 52 flows into the water collecting tank 41"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102747240-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, even if a rainwater blocking tent (60) and frame (61) are not installed in the car wash section (10) of the car wash, there is an effect of resolving the problem of overload caused by rainwater flowing into the wastewater storage tank (30)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102747240-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "therefore, to block the inflow of rainwater into the wastewater storage tank (30), the above-described rainwater inflow prevention device (100) is installed in the middle of the wastewater inlet pipe (40)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200208312-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the sediment is separated by stages through the fine holes of the primary filtration network and the bottom plate to provide a rainwater catchment for the road equipped with a filtration tank to prevent the drainage blockage in advance"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584236-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "however, even with this method, it is difficult to completely remove the harmful contaminants that are strongly attached to the catchment surface by hydrophobic interaction, and the accumulated contaminants are gradually introduced into the storage tank over a long period of time during rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584236-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "thus, when rainwater is concentrated on the catchment surface 2 in which contamination by contaminants is prevented early by the titanium dioxide photocatalyst layer, the rainwater is transferred to the storage tank 1 through the catchment port 3 and stored"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the treated water through which the contaminant is removed by passing through the filter medium filling tank 71 is accommodated in the discharge box 91 by overflowing through the discharge unit 90, and then introduced into the drain pipe or artificial wetland through the drainage path 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100614766-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "therefore, in the present invention, the removal of contaminants is actively performed on the road drainage during the initial rainfall stage in which the content of the pollutants is high, and the filter filling tank 71 considering the low amount of pollutants in the subsequent road drainage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100750645-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is provided in the storage space of the treatment tank 6 includes a filtration device (9) for filtering and adsorption to remove contaminants contained in the road surface drainage rising from the lower portion of the treatment tank (6)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100823240-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, when the initial rainwater and sediment contaminants are completely excluded from the initial rainwater treatment facility 1 and the pressure or water level becomes zero, the drain pump 21 receiving the water is driven to operate the water tank 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100927631-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, when rainwater flows into the sedimentation tank 200, heavy foreign matter such as sand sinks to the bottom and light foreign matter such as leaves or vinyl fragments rises on the surface of the water to easily remove contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100962546-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, the contaminants accumulated on the bottom surface of the sediment holding tank 410 may be prevented from rising to the filter plate accommodating part 160 by riding the drain pipe 420"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100962546-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, particulate contaminants contained in rainwater fall into the sediment holding tank 410 and is confined"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101113989-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, since the tip of the connecting pipe 50 is bent downward so as to be submerged in the rainwater in the sedimentation tank 10, contaminants having a small specific gravity such as oil floating on the water surface may not pass through the connecting pipe 50"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101181324-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, after treating the roadbed sediment and sediment contaminants contained in the sewage of rainy weather has been developed and used to flow into natural rivers or nearby sea, there is a storage tank type treatment device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101219791-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "the method of claim 1, non-contaminant purification device characterized in that it further comprises a filtration tank connected to the rain pipe and the rainwater flowing through the flow passage of the rain pipe flows to remove foreign substances piggybacked in rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101273679-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a contaminant separation tank 200 installed at a downstream side of the water collecting facility 100 to remove particulate contaminants from the rainwater collected by the water collecting facility 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101273679-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a contaminant separation tank 200 installed at a downstream side of the water collecting facility 100 to remove particulate contaminants from the rainwater collected by the water collecting facility 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101323288-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, rainwater and contaminants from the side of the road 1 flow together through these steel gratings 102 and 104 and are then stored in the settling tank 110"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101323288-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this way, in order to remove the sedimentary contaminants introduced with the rain water, the filter 120 is separated from the bottom 116 of the sedimentation tank 110 to perform the cleaning operation of the filter 120, and then coupled to the original position"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101323288-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as shown, the primary penetrating paper 130 is positioned side by side with the settling tank 110, to remove and remove the floating contaminants primarily in the rainwater flowing over from the settling tank 110"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101323288-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as shown, the primary penetrating basin 230 is located side by side with the settling tank 210, to remove and remove the floating contaminants primarily in the rainwater flowing over from the settling tank 210"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101358438-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the filtration tank 50 is supplied with rainwater from which sand and oil have been removed from the sedimentation tank 40, and various foreign matters contained in the rainwater [such as foreign matters of fine particles, etc., which are not sorted in the contaminant separator 20 and the sedimentation tank 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101382006-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in detail, the purification treatment tank 10 removes the fine turbidity contaminants or soluble contaminants contained in the rainwater passing through the precipitation tank 20 and the precipitation tank 20 removing the floating contaminants and the suspended solids from the rainwater"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102060940-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "to provide a rainwater storage and water treatment system using a multi-stage rainwater storage tank that is easy to clean the removed contaminants separately"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102060940-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the present invention is to provide a rainwater storage and water treatment system using a multi-stage rainwater storage tank that can effectively remove contaminants contained in the rainwater in the process of collecting rainwater, and easy to clean the removed contaminants separately"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "(2) since the filter which removes contaminants contained in the drainage by filtration or adsorption is installed in the treatment tank, the drainage flowed into the inlet of the storm drain flows through the flow path including the maintenance tank and the treatment tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200357071-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "road drainage with first flush treatment ability the present invention is to insert a filter filling tank having a filtration treatment function in the conventional rainwater receiver to the road surface drainage treatment device having an initial excellent treatment function that can reliably remove and treat contaminants contained in the road surface drainage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200357071-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the treated water through which the contaminant is removed by passing through the filter medium filling tank 71 is accommodated in the discharge box 91 by overflowing through the discharge unit 90, and then introduced into the drain pipe or artificial wetland through the drainage path 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200358330-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a filtration member provided in the treatment tank and configured to filter and adsorb and remove contaminants contained in road surface drainage passing from an upper portion of the treatment tank to a lower side"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200358330-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the present invention actively removes contaminants from road surface drainage during the initial rainfall stage with high content of contaminants, and the contaminant content is less for road drainage than the treatment capacity in the subsequent treatment tank 20"}, {"pat_id": "US-8661819-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the contaminants may be removed from the heat exchanger in a generally non-invasive manner by periodically discharging water with the highly concentrated contaminants from a bottom drain of the heat exchanger (e.g., blow-down, blow-by, etc.) and directing the water to a containment location (e.g., evaporation pond or heat exchanger, storage tank etc.)"}, {"pat_id": "US-8776522-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the contaminants may be removed from the heat exchanger in a generally non-invasive manner by periodically discharging water with the highly concentrated contaminants from a bottom drain of the heat exchanger (e.g., blow-down, blow-by, etc.) and directing the water to a containment location (e.g., evaporation pond or heat exchanger, storage tank etc.)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100584236-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "thus, when rainwater is concentrated on the catchment surface 2 in which contamination by contaminants is prevented early by the titanium dioxide photocatalyst layer, the rainwater is transferred to the storage tank 1 through the catchment port 3 and stored"}, {"pat_id": "US-5736059-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the tank must therefore drain away into the lower heat exchanger and thence to the sewer when there is no wastewater flow, leaving the upper heat exchanger high and dry protecting the fresh water supply from contamination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101170311-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the initial rainfall storage tank 21 may be made of any one material selected from iron, stainless steel, polyethylene (pe) or concrete so as to prevent corrosion and damage caused by contaminants contained in the initial rainfall"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102809593-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, it is a system that physically stores filtered rainwater in a rainwater storage tank without electronic devices by utilizing the gravity of falling rainwater, thereby reducing maintenance costs and providing a physical rainwater utilization system that does not require frequent maintenance due to corrosion or damage"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100955909-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, in order to solve the problem that the contaminants accumulated in the inflow tank decay and cause odor after the rainfall is over, the hole is drilled at the bottom of the inflow tank, and gravel or porous media is installed outside to filter the contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100985170-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, in order to solve the problem that the contaminants accumulated in the inflow tank decay and cause odor after the rainfall is over, the hole is drilled at the bottom of the inflow tank, and gravel or porous media is installed outside to filter the contaminants"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100800335-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "substantially, the rainwater treatment tank 22 is not likely to have the same internal diameter of the rainwater treatment tank 22 that is mass produced due to the high probability of shrinkage or deformation during drying (cooling), and the index plate 14 is coupled"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100350735-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, during rainfall, the amount of sewage inflow is high and the flow rate is fast, so that the soil is not deposited in the sedimentation tank and flows into the dwelling house as it is, so that the cross section of the dwelling house 3 is reduced and the sewage terminal treatment plant is caused"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101056650-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "here, the drain valve 158 is frequently opened to remove foreign substances when the rainwater reservoir tank 150 is cleaned or when foreign substances are deposited at the bottom"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200171293-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, during rainfall, the amount of sewage inflow is high and the flow rate is fast, so that the soil is not deposited in the sedimentation tank and flows into the dwelling house as it is, so that the cross section of the dwelling house 3 is reduced and the sewage terminal treatment plant is caused"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100875260-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the case of such a buried water tank, the water tank is not affected by the external temperature as compared to the water tank installed on the ground and is not affected by the external environment such as rain or dust, and in particular, the water in the winter water tank is prevented from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100942717-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "insulation material (10ac) is filled in the separation space formed between the first plate (10aa) and the second plate (10ab) can be used in the form of urethane, the winter of the water tank (10) by the temperature drop outside, such as it prevents freezing of rainwater stored inside to prevent the collection tank 10 from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4029133-B2", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "it is possible to prevent the water in the water storage tank 2 from leaking, and it is possible to surely switch between water storage and water discharge by opening and closing the drain hole 11c with the drain hole opening / closing lid 13"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102041291-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in order to solve this problem, a number of techniques have been disclosed for preventing leakage of odor flowing back from the sewage pipe back to the rainwater pipe or rainwater collection tank, for example, to cover oil and access holes of the rainwater collection tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102041291-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "however, only the mechanical devices installed in rainwater pipes or storm water collection tanks do not completely prevent leakage of odors flowing back from the sewage pipes, and as a result, odor leaks around sewage pipes or storm water collection tanks, causing discomfort to passers-by"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102041291-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "odor leak prevention deodorization system 100 of the rainwater collection tank of the present invention is installed in the rainwater collection tank (5)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102041291-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "operation control for a time to remove the odor by the chemical reaction by ozone, but there is a risk that some of the odor may leak around the rainwater collection tank in the early stage of operation because the time required to reduce the odor by the chemical reaction of ozone and odor"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102216793-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as described above, after removing the collecting plate 28 and the sensor 25, when the handle 29 of the top tank 12 is lifted and lifted, the inlet of the lower tank 12 from the drain 19 of the upper tank 12 as