e reverse contact oxidation method, a water barrier is formed in the middle of the river to introduce the river water into the primary storage tank, and when the rainfall increases, the river is discharged to discharge the river water to protect the river water purification device"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100381901-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the general water purification apparatus by the catalytic oxidation method includes a primary storage tank that collects contaminated river water with various wastewater discharged from a home, a factory, or a non-point source, and removes sludge that is settled"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102816086-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the river water to be treated, which has passed through the pretreatment unit (10), flows into the biological contact oxidation treatment unit (30), is purified in the biological contact oxidation treatment unit (30), and then passes through the discharge tank (40) to be discharged into a river or lake, thereby performing the functions of water quality purification and management during normal times"}, {"pat_id": "JP-4377451-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "therefore, in such an aerobic sewage purification apparatus, in particular, when an abnormality occurs in the blower, the inside of the septic tank cannot be maintained in a normal aerobic condition, the purification function is lowered, and untreated water from the septic tank to the river is discharged and becomes environmental pollution"}, {"pat_id": "US-10865547-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in extraordinary storm events, these surge tanks can easily become overwhelmed, thus requiring the release of untreated water (sewage and stromwater) to a river, bay, etc., or even bypassing the stormwater collection tank(s) altogether"}, {"pat_id": "US-11603651-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in extraordinary storm events, these surge tanks can easily become overwhelmed, thus requiring the release of untreated water (sewage and stormwater) to a river, b