  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101002203-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "if the measured residual salinity is less than 0.2 ppm, it is determined that a considerable amount of contaminants remain in the membrane filter 20 (s40), and the controller 60 increases the amount of chlorine supplied in the flame tank 40 (s50)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102425449-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "from this point of view, it can be seen that the salinity content (or concentration of other contaminants) of the seed water inside the storage tank increases as evaporation occurs"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101695898-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "field of the invention the present invention relates to a water tank for sewage treatment in the field of sewage treatment technology, and more particularly, to a water tank for sewage treatment with improved salinity resistance and corrosion resistance while improving sewage treatment efficiency"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101695898-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "1, 2006) water tank for sewage treatment summary of the invention the present invention has been made in view of the above-described problems in the prior art, and an object of the present invention is to provide a water tank for sewage treatment which is improved in salinity resistance and corrosion resistance while improving sewage treatment efficiency"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102129684-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "in addition, since the salt concentration control tank supplies the wastewater with the adjusted salt concentration to the treatment tank, it is possible to keep the width of the change in the salt concentration of the wastewater flowing into the treatment tank to be small, thereby preventing degradation of microorganisms due to salinity in the treatment tank, resulting in treatment"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101862825-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "an electrolysis tank for electrolyzing the mixed water supplied from the salinity dilution module to produce sodium hypochlorite"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100952911-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the sea water is gradually evaporated to increase the salinity, and the salt water is increased to supply the ballast tank 110 through the seawater supply pipe 130 to increase the salinity of the ballast water to lower the freezing point"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100952911-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as such, the salinity of which salinity is increased is introduced into the ballast tank 110 through the seawater supply pipe 130 as in the above method, thereby lowering the freezing point of the ballast water"}]</data>
