ined in the storm and fine contaminants are removed from the stormwater inflow pipe 140 of the storage tank 100"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101741449-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the inlet tank 100 is formed with a screen box 120 to remove contaminants from the storm water discharged from the inlet pipe 110 and is formed at a lower side of the screen box 120, the desulphurization tool 130 is formed to have a flow regulating function"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "(2) since the filter which removes contaminants contained in the drainage by filtration or adsorption is installed in the treatment tank, the drainage flowed into the inlet of the storm drain flows through the flow path including the maintenance tank and the treatment tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101879690-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the stormwater inflow pipe 11 is arranged on the ceiling portion above the discharge chamber 14 of the collecting tank 10 and the discharge pipe 12 is arranged on the bottom portion of the discharge chamber 14 therefore, the stormwater flowing through the storm inflow pipe 11 is quickly discharged through the discharge pipe 12 when the initial storm water is excluded, and the initial stormwater with high contamination degree is discharged to the buoyancy chamber 15 )"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101202895-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "meanwhile, the septic tank 30 has a series of decaying tanks 31, filtration tanks 32, an oxidizing tank 33, and a disinfection tank 34 so that the initial rainwater introduced into the stormwater chamber 210 can be sequentially purified"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101382006-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "accordingly, the initial stormwater treatment apparatus 1 of the present invention quickly discharges rainwater, that is, residual water remaining in the purification treatment tank 10, to prevent the residual water from decaying"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as a result, deposits absorbing contaminants are deposited in the mud at the bottom of the storm receiver 20, the maintenance tank 30, and the treatment tank 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200343186-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the other hand, if the removal process of the contaminants continues, the bottom of the storm receiver 20, the maintenance tank 30 and the treatment tank 40, deposits containing contaminants are deposited, and the filter medium filling tank ( 70) contaminants will also collect inside, and regular removal will be required"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101224380-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, in the field, problems such as securing convenience of pc block assembly construction, securing structural stability of storm water storage tanks constructed by pc block assembly, problems of leaking through gaps between blocks and removing sludge accumulated inside storm water storage tanks are pointed out"}, {"pat_id": "US-10865547-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the event of a truly significant rain (storm) event, these storage tanks can be overwhelmed, thus resulting in flooding or discharge of excess storm water to the sewage treatment system, a body of water, or a river"}, {"pat_id": "US-10865547-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in extraordinary storm events, these surge tanks can easily become overwhelmed, thus requiring the release of untreated water (sewage and stromwater) to a river, bay, etc., or even bypassing the stormwater collection tank(s) altogether"}, {"pat_id": "US-11603651-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the event of a truly significant rain (storm) event, these storage tanks can be overwhelmed, thus resulting in flooding or discharge of excess storm water to the sewage treatment system, a body of water, or a river"}, {"pat_id": "US-11603651-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in extraordinary storm events, these surge tanks can easily become overwhelmed, thus requiring the release of untreated water (sewage and stormwater) to a river, bay, etc., or even bypassing the stormwater collection tank(s) altogether"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200324955-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when it rains, the sewage is treated in the same way as above, and the rainwater that is exceeding the sewage treatment amount (exactly diluted sewage mixed with rainwater) is pumped by the rainwater transfer pump (bar), and the rainwater distribution tank (3) next, the supernatant is precipitated in the storm sedimentation basin (5)"}, {"pat_id": "US-7022243-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the event of a heavy storm where there is a high flow of storm water, the separation tank 10 of the present invention also functions to convey the additional flow of water into a separate high flow treatment chamber so as to circumvent the second treatment chamber 36 thereby preventing any scour or resuspension of previously captured material from the second chamber and filter/recharge chamber"}, {"pat_id": "US-10865547-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in extraordinary storm events, these surge tanks can easily become overwhelmed, thus requiring the release of untreated water (sewage and stromwater) to a river, bay, etc., or even bypassing the stormwater collection tank(s) altogether"}, {"pat_id": "US-11603651-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in extraordinary storm events, these surge tanks can easily become overwhelmed, thus requiring the release of untreated water (sewage and stormwater) to a river, bay, etc., or even bypassing the stormwater collection tank(s) altogether"}]</data>
