  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101368425-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, the first cover 20 and the second cover 30 is provided to cover the opening of the water tank 10 to prevent the inflow of foreign matter and infiltration of bacteria in the air, the first cover 20 the space between the second cover 30 serves as a thermal insulation space to block the influence of the external temperature of the water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101368425-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as such, the first cover 200 covers the opening of the water tank 100 to prevent the inflow of foreign substances and the penetration of bacteria in the air, and the space between the first cover 200 and the second cover 300 is it functions as an insulated space to block the influence of the outside temperature of the water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0161642-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, when a backflow occurs from the hot water storage tank 12 due to the breakage of the check valve 13, the temperature of the cold water of the cold water storage tank 10 is increased to be higher than the minimum cooling temperature"}, {"pat_id": "US-4204956-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by the provision of a quartz jacket about each uv lamp, the possibility of lamp breakage in the tank is materially reduced, and also the jackets provide for the lamps to be operated at desired temperatures for optimum radiation whatever the temperature of water passing through the system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102883227-B1", "para_id": "claim_7", "text": "a wastewater storage facility where wastewater containing ammonia is stored, a cavitation generating device that receives wastewater discharged from the above wastewater storage tank and generates cavitation to increase the temperature of wastewater containing ammonia"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102036529-B1", "para_id": "para_12", "text": "after checking only the temperature of the water inside the water tank (1) to determine the operation of the heater member 20 as the temperature inside the water tank (1) or less than 4"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100328970-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the circumferential surface of the hopper tank is characterized in that a constant temperature wire coil is attached to prevent freezing of the contaminants in the hopper tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101693100-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in the above-described embodiment, although the water treatment system has determined to perform the chemical cleaning when the contamination index of the membrane filtration tank is equal to or greater than the second value, in another embodiment, the chemical washing is performed according to at least one of the temperature, as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102085280-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "on the contrary, in the case where the mlss concentration is increased, the wastewater temperature in the tank is maintained at about 30 to 40 c during the biological treatment in the liquid corrosion tank, which is caused by the difference between the external temperature and the air supplied into the tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101151121-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this way, by crushing and homogenizing the organic sludge, it is possible to reduce the temperature, pressure, reaction time and the like in the subsequent reaction tank 5"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100315762-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the present invention, the composite panel 10 can be firmly assembled by fitting the composite panel 10 to the skeleton constituting each component panel of the large tank, so that the connection part of the composite panel 10 is caused by internal deformation pressure due to bending deformation or temperature change"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100988365-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the concrete tank exhibits deformation due to temperature deterioration, the cracks may occur in the panel adhesive composition of the concrete tank, resulting in a decrease in waterproofness and separation of the panel and the adhesive composition"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100271942-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "or higher, it is possible to prevent efficiency degradation such as nitrification reaction due to low outside air temperature during subsequent processing in the aeration tank 60"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200454214-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a heat exchanger provided with a coil or plate type softening line to increase the temperature of soft water by heat exchange between soft water supplied from a softener and sodium hypochlorite flowing from the electrolysis tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200454214-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a heat exchanger provided with a coil or plate type softening line to increase the temperature of soft water by heat exchange between soft water supplied from a softener and sodium hypochlorite flowing from the electrolysis tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "under the control of the drive means and the control means, the temperature of the cold water tank is raised to prevent freezing of the cold water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the present invention has been made to solve the above problems, an object of the present invention is to determine the freezing of the cold water tank according to the changing product internal temperature and cold water temperature to determine the freezing of the cold water tank even in the winter at low room temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "four-way valve driving means for driving control of the four-way valve to prevent freezing of the cold water tank, it is characterized in that the compressor driving means for controlling the drive to increase the temperature of the cold water tank according to the control to prevent freezing of the cold water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is determined whether or not the preset ice generating temperature tcd (cold water temperature at which freezing occurs in the cold water tank)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "according to the temperature control apparatus and the method of the cold / hot water purifier according to the present invention as described above, it is determined whether the cold water tank is freezing according to the changing product internal temperature and the cold water temperature, so that the cold water tank freezes even in the winter when the room temperature is low"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100634761-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when it is determined that the communication state is good, the temperature data of the water tank together with the ambient temperature data (which can determine the possibility of freezing of the water pipe, measured by the temperature sensor) and (if the pump abnormality can be determined) preferably, a current sensor is further provided to control the pump using the current data supplied to the pump"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100901209-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "according to this aspect of the present invention, the water supply control device checks the outside air temperature sensed by the temperature sensor and intermittently drives the pump to prevent freezing of the water supply pipe supplying water to the water tank of the drain"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101194148-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "if the temperature is lowered, the outdoor temperature may not directly affect the water tank, thus delaying the freezing time"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102065694-B1", "para_id": "para_8", "text": "thus, when the temperature of the storage tank 100 is below a certain temperature, the freezing prevention function operates"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102344740-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "maintaining the temperature of the purified water flowing into and stored in the purified water tank unit 1100 by the anti-freezing heater unit 1600 at any one temperature selected from the range of 27 to 75 degrees celsius is to promote the activation of the advanced oxidation process (aop)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200468890-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the user can adjust the temperature controller 32 so that the water (w) heating temperature in the steam tank 10 can be arbitrarily set to be heated, whereby the water (w) appropriately according to the freezing state of the freezing pipe"}, {"pat_id": "US-4784173-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when freezing temperatures are sensed by the bulb, there is an outflow of water from the valve device and an inflow of water from the inlet conduit, thereby preventing freezing of water within the tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-4936114-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "sufficient aqueous ice slurry is fed to mixing tank 22 by conduit 54 to keep the temperature of the liquid therein close to, but above, the freezing point so that there is no increase in ice particle formation"}, {"pat_id": "US-8141584-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in colder environments, existing exterior collection and storage tanks may crack or break when the temperature drops below freezing, and the water in the tank turns to ice"}, {"pat_id": "US-8141584-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the temperature of the water in the storage tank falls below a specified temperature for a specified period of time, thereby indicating that the possibility of freezing exists, the microprocessor activates the pump to dump water from the storage tank through the alternate outlet to the alternate destination"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101861072-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the thermal hydrolysis apparatus 65 is operated to remove the concentrated sludge from the sludge concentration tank 60 under conditions of high temperature (about 150 c) and high pressure (about 20 bar) to methane fermentation of the post-"}, {"pat_id": "US-6814866-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the typical net result is that on average the temperature in the influence zone can be expected to be above the temperature in like soil remote from the leaching system, principally attributable to the heat content of the waste water from the septic tank source"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in the illustrated embodiment of the tank water heater 10 and the alternative embodiment of the tankless water heater, if the temperature of condensate is equal to or close to the temperature of room air, the controller 142 determines at box 245 that there is no leakage of water (from the tank 14, or from the heat exchanger coil in the alternative embodiment)"}, {"pat_id": "US-8403000-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "tank heat leak has a dramatic effect on the pressure temperature and density relationships of the lng thus making it very difficult to control the fuel tank pressure and maintain consistent fuel quality for delivery to the engine"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3779320-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in the illustrated embodiment of the tank water heater 10 and the alternative embodiment of the tankless water heater, if the temperature of condensate is equal to or close to the temperature of room air, the controller 142 determines at box 245 that there is no leakage of water (from the tank 14, or from the heat exchanger coil in the alternative embodiment)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101240216-B1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "an aerobic digestion tank 100 in which organic matter contained in waste water is oxidatively decomposed by activation of high temperature aerobic microorganisms, and an air nozzle provided at an inner lower portion of the aerobic digestion tank 100 to discharge air providing a lifting force for circulating the waste water"}, {"pat_id": "JP-3672455-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however, since the activity of iron bacteria, that is, the oxidation amount of iron may change due to the influence of temperature, the measuring tank 10 is maintained at a temperature at which the activity of iron bacteria is stabilized by the temperature regulator 5"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100953075-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, latent heat is scattered with water vapor during the dropping to evaporate the organic oxidation heat and the denitrification heat, and the temperature of the microorganism activity of the oxidizing tank is changed to the atmospheric temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101265963-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "comprising an apparatus for maintaining a reaction temperature in an aerobic tank, and forming an optimum reaction condition in the aerobic tank even with an external temperature change, thereby improving the efficiency of organic matter oxidation and nitrification and thereby stable discharge"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101642081-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, even when only the oxidizing agent is supplied to the regeneration wastewater purification tank 140 during purification of regeneration wastewater, on the other hand, if the temperature of the regeneration wastewater is lower than the reference temperature, the oxidizing efficiency of the oxidizing agent is lowered, so that it is required to supply the reaction catalyst for promoting the oxidation reaction in addition to the oxidizing agent"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102344740-B1", "para_id": "para_10", "text": "maintaining the temperature of the purified water flowing into and stored in the purified water tank unit 1100 by the anti-freezing heater unit 1600 at any one temperature selected from the range of 27 to 75 degrees celsius is to promote the activation of the advanced oxidation process (aop)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101232378-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as such, the water tank 120 is installed in the air in the inner space and heats only a limited amount of the internal air to a temperature higher than the freezing point in the state of good heat shielding with the outside, thereby maintaining a small amount to prevent freezing of the stored water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200454214-Y1", "para_id": "claim_1", "text": "a heat exchanger provided with a coil or plate type softening line to increase the temperature of soft water by heat exchange between soft water supplied from a softener and sodium hypochlorite flowing from the electrolysis tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200454214-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "a heat exchanger provided with a coil or plate type softening line to increase the temperature of soft water by heat exchange between soft water supplied from a softener and sodium hypochlorite flowing from the electrolysis tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101519389-B1", "para_id": "para_7", "text": "when the dehydrated cake, the additive, and the moisture control agent (swelling agent) are mixed in the mixer 500 and supplied to the fermentation tank 503 of the fermentation process in the primary dehydration process and the secondary dehydration process, co 2 , h 2 o, and nh 3 , the temperature increases to 60-70 c due to the heat of reaction"}]</data>
