  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-0137696-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "moreover, the method of checking the low water level in the water tank by using the air tank is very conventional, and it only functions to block the flow of water only when the water is almost full in the water tank, thereby making it difficult to identify the low water amount in the water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100546851-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in the control unit 90, when the second filter material 22a of the second filter tank 20 is blocked and the water level is increased, the water flows back through the overflow pipe 45, and this is applied to the detection signal of the second water level sensor 22b"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100546851-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the control unit 90 is blocked by the second filter material 22a of the second filter tank 20 when the water level is increased, the water flows back through the overflow pipe 45, by the detection signal of the second water level sensor 22b the operation of the inflow pump 70 is stopped"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101000865-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, when the pressurized water tank reaches the minimum water level, the disk interlocked with the buckle automatically descends to close the flow path of the water cylinder connected to the water supply and drain pipe, thereby blocking the air pressure from leaking to the outside through the water supply and drain pipe"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101388033-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the water level of the sewage stored in the tank 30 rises and the height of the buckle member 54 increases, the wire 56b is pulled up by the load of the sensing block 56c and the sensing block 56c is lowered"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102400040-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the water level of the treated water tank is measured in real time, and when the water level is out of a certain range, the gate valve is selectively opened and closed to block the flow path of the overflow pipe, thereby increasing the overflow height of the treatment tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200332116-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "at this time, when the water tank level is a high water level, the flow of water is blocked by the float 42 and the pressure valve 43, so that the current of the pump motor increases without being stabilized as shown in fig"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100499785-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "the controller 64 is difficult to supply water to the water tank 10 due to a failure of the pump 3a or a blockage of the reverse osmosis filter 7 when the lower limit water level detection signal is input for a predetermined time or more among the water level detection signals sh"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100540762-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the controller 64 is difficult to supply water to the water tank 10 due to a failure of the pump 3a or a blockage of the reverse osmosis filter 7 when the lower limit water level detection signal is input for a predetermined time or more among the water level detection signals sh"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100841664-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "the fifth water level sensor 45 detects an overflow phenomenon that occurs when the water level in the electrolytic cell 30 is increased due to a blockage of the outlet 27a or the like, which is not drained or an increase in inflow from the storage tank 20"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101054375-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the fifth water level sensor 45 detects an overflow phenomenon that occurs when the water level in the electrolytic cell 30 is increased due to a blockage of the outlet port 27a or the like, which is not drained or an increase in inflow from the storage tank 20 increases"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101220540-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "that is, when the water level in the pressure tank 314 is increased because the pressurized water does not flow smoothly into the flotation tank 200 due to the blockage of the microbubble injection unit 320, the water level sensor 334 detects the pump 312"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101272800-B1", "para_id": "claim_6", "text": "the method of claim 1, the compressed air supply means provides a compressed air shock wave to the filtration filter according to the state of the reservoir tank level of the water level detector to eliminate the blockage of the filtration filter, or to provide a compressed air shock wave periodically or occasionally to prevent the blockage of the filtration filter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101272800-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the compressed air supply means provides a compressed air shock wave to the filtration filter according to the state of the reservoir tank level of the water level detector to eliminate the blockage of the filtration filter, or to provide a compressed air shock wave periodically or occasionally to prevent the blockage of the filtration filter"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200365284-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the controller 64 is difficult to supply water to the water tank 10 due to a failure of the pump 3a or a blockage of the reverse osmosis filter 7 when the lower limit water level detection signal is input for a predetermined time or more among the water level detection signals sh"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101729735-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "field of the invention [0001] the present invention relates to a water level elevating device for a water-the present invention relates to a water level elevating device, and more particularly, to a water level elevating device for a water pipe turning method applied to a water turning method bypassing a work section of a sub tank for maintenance or monitoring of a sub tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101036584-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the water level of the sludge storage tank 100 increases above a predetermined level, the flow rate controller 110 increases the output of the transfer pump 107 to increase the flow amount of sludge transferred to the cavitation storage tank 120, and the sludge storage tank 100"}, {"pa