 contamination level is also increased"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100823240-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, when the initial rainwater and sediment contaminants are completely excluded from the initial rainwater treatment facility 1 and the pressure or water level becomes zero, the drain pump 21 receiving the water is driven to operate the water tank 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101130918-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, the present invention by installing the filtration device 200 in the position as described above, the contaminants in the water discharged through the drain pipe 120 from the swimming pool to be filtered immediately before passing through the water level control tank (300)"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101322190-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "therefore, when the purified treatment water from which the contaminants have been removed through the purification treatment water recovery pipe 140 provided in the internal treatment tank 200 of the present invention is recovered, the amount corresponding to the purification treatment water by the water level detection means and the control unit 600"}, {"pat_id": "JP-5042805-B2", "para_id": "para_21", "text": "specifically, when the water level gauge 111 detects that the water level in the contaminant removal tank 110 is higher than the specified water level, control is performed to relatively increase the amount of water transferred by the advection pump 122, and the contamination level is also increased"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101291991-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in this case, the water level in the production water tank 5 reaches the water level l even after the operation time set to sufficiently remove the corrosion promoting component in the feed water as described above to prevent the deterioration of the water quality"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102500623-B1", "para_id": "para_17", "text": "an anti-corrosion coating is applied to the outer periphery of the lower part installed inside the wastewater treatment tank 100 to measure the water level inside the tank and prevent corrosion by the sterilizing solution"}, {"pat_id": "KR-200167943-Y1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "according to one feature of the automatic water supply device of the present invention, both the discharge valve and the water level valve installed in the water tank are made of plastic and rubber packing to prevent rust or corrosion and to have durability"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101500632-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "(f2 f3) accordingly, in the present invention, the amount of water stored in the water tank is automatically adjusted to a level higher than the water level capable of detecting a wind speed (wind load) this is to prevent defects due to wind loads such as overturning and partial crushing of the water tank due to insufficient amount of water stored in the water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100331066-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by equaling the water level in groups, the concrete capacity of decaying tanks is reduced and the simultaneous treatment efficiency is maximized"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101113083-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in addition, the pump well 46 operates the transfer pump when a certain water level is reached while storing the treated water discharged from the organic material decay reaction tank 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101113090-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, the pump well 46 is provided with a transfer pump that operates when the predetermined water level is reached while storing the treated water discharged from the organic material decay reaction tank 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101113090-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in addition, the pump well 46 operates the transfer pump when a certain water level is reached while storing the treated water discharged from the organic material decay reaction tank 40"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102783510-B1", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "when the water level of the rainwater storage tank (200) reaches the minimum water level (h2), t