  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "KR-101254083-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the water level of the groundwater well is changed according to the operation of the water pump (m), the sewage blocking air valve 40 is kept open so that air flows in and out of the groundwater, and the groundwater pollution prevention device is flooded by flooding or the like"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101254083-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "since the valve spool 42 is always buoyant in the submerged state, the close contact surface 42a of the valve spool 42 remains in close contact with the seat surface 41b of the valve cylinder 41, and thus the air passage 41a of the valve cylinder 41 is blocked, and the surface water due to the flooding is blocked from flowing into the groundwater well"}, {"pat_id": "US-11560697-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "without proper maintenance, backwater valves can become blocked or stuck, giving building managers and homeowners a false sense of security that they will be protected during a flooding event"}, {"pat_id": "US-11560697-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however many homeowners and residents are not aware of the presence or operation of a backwater valve, and if the valve is closed due to a flooding event or blockage many residents will not be aware of it until sanitary sewage begins flowing back into their building"}, {"pat_id": "US-11560697-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "however many homeowners and residents are not aware of the presence or operation of a backwater valve, and if the valve is closed due to a flooding event or blockage many residents will not be aware of it until sanitary sewage begins flowing back into their building"}, {"pat_id": "EP-2749860-B1", "para_id": "para_9", "text": "the signal interruption takes place at an open main valve 5 for the purpose of targeted water removal from the hydrant 1 or in case of leak, a defective main valve 5, or with a closed main valve 5, if the drainage aperture 116 penetrates through the drainage sheet 118 and in the hydrant 1 waste water as a result of flooding"}, {"pat_id": "US-10214881-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "description of the related art currently, commercial and residential commodes suffer from leaks due to worn or stuck flapper valves and defective fill valves which cause unnecessary water loss, water consumption, and flooding"}, {"pat_id": "US-11905688-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "the shutoff valve 532 can be used to prevent flooding for leaks downstream of the water device 120"}, {"pat_id": "US-4659063-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "description of the prior art there are many systems for automatically controlling a valve to interrupt the water supply in the event that flooding occurs due to a leak somewhere in a water system"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100439852-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "by the way, the water flowing through the water pipe is also transported with foreign matters lighter than water, and these foreign matters are adsorbed by the air valve and the distillation valve to form a gap and cause an accident such as leakage and flooding"}, {"pat_id": "US-7802587-B1", "para_id": "para_27", "text": "with valve 10 closed no further water will be permitted to pass from drain pipe 53 into sump pit 50, thereby preventing basement 61 from flooding"}, {"pat_id": "US-10214881-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "description of the related art currently, commercial and residential commodes suffer from leaks due to worn or stuck flapper valves and defective fill valves which cause unnecessary water loss, water consumption, and flooding"}]</data>
