  <data key="d7">[{"pat_id": "US-11325845-B2", "para_id": "para_4", "text": "a blowdown temperature control loop may be initialized and an extra source valve command cap may be determined in block 8018 as well"}, {"pat_id": "US-11352267-B2", "para_id": "para_5", "text": "a blowdown temperature control loop may be initialized and an extra source valve command cap may be determined in block 8018 as well"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0161642-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "therefore, when a backflow occurs from the hot water storage tank 12 due to the breakage of the check valve 13, the temperature of the cold water of the cold water storage tank 10 is increased to be higher than the minimum cooling temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100806134-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is composed of a double wall having a minimum temperature difference between the ground and the valve chamber structure 10 to prevent condensation inside the valve chamber structure 10 to prevent corrosion of the valve facility 110 disposed in the valve chamber structure 10"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101804811-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in addition, since the sandwich panel 90 used in the temporary end water service valve chamber 1 according to the present invention can prevent condensation caused by a difference in temperature from the outside, corrosion of the mechanical structure can be prevented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101804812-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in addition, since the sandwich panel 90 used in the temporary end water service valve chamber 1 according to the present invention can prevent condensation caused by a difference in temperature from the outside, corrosion of the mechanical structure can be prevented"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102196538-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "meanwhile, when the chamber 10 is buried in the ground, condensation is generated in the wall plate 12 due to a temperature difference between the pipe and the underground, and such condensation occurs along the wall plate 12 of the chamber 10 and the bottom plate 13 it becomes a factor of failure due to corrosion of various valves and measuring instruments"}, {"pat_id": "US-9810377-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in addition, temperature fluctuations will be induced both during the pressure decay when the isolation valve is closed and then again during the pressure increase when the isolation valve is opened"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102733651-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "this structure adopts the advantages of a wedge gate valve (413) and a parallel gate valve (416), and is relatively less affected by deformation due to temperature and pressure"}, {"pat_id": "KR-101395863-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when there is a request for the alkaline ionized water at a normal room temperature, the flow control valve 150 is filtered by the water filter 110 to convert the general purified water bypassed through the bypass pipe 130 to the electrolytic water and is supplied to the alkaline ion electrolysis chamber 142 where the alkaline ionized water will be produced and the acidic ion electrolysis chamber 144 where the acidic ionized water will be produced"}, {"pat_id": "US-10914393-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "in one particular embodiment, the radial extension can be configured to move beyond the flow restriction of the seat opening to provide a third stage where flow through the automated valve is increased at higher temperatures"}, {"pat_id": "EP-0527545-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "as the ambient temperature has dropped to about 5 c or below, the first valve is heated by a heater in which it is housed, thereby preventing its freezing"}, {"pat_id": "KR-0175895-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "four-way valve driving means for driving control of the four-way valve to prevent freezing of the cold water tank, it is characterized in that the compressor driving means for controlling the drive to increase the temperature of the cold water tank according to the control to prevent freezing of the cold water tank"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100991888-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, the controller c opens the first opening / closing valve v\u2081 and simultaneously shuts off the second opening / closing valve v2 when the temperature sensor 13 detects the expected temperature of the freezing wave"}, {"pat_id": "US-11066813-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the temperature drops, the system opens the main valve and allows the water to flow, thus preventing the pipe from freezing"}, {"pat_id": "US-4763682-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the valve closing element of this patent is caused to open said valve and allow the drainage of fluid from a connected pipe in response to temperatures approaching the freezing point"}, {"pat_id": "US-4763682-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "it is therefore seen that the present invention provides a simple device for activating a fluid valve in response to a thermal, and specifically, to a freezing, change in temperature, without the requirement for external power or human intervention"}, {"pat_id": "US-4784173-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when freezing temperatures are sensed by the bulb, there is an outflow of water from the valve device and an inflow of water from the inlet conduit, thereby preventing freezing of water within the tank"}, {"pat_id": "US-4784173-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "thus, there is a need for a completely failure-safe freeze prevention valve that is useful under industrial conditions, automatically responsive to freezing temperatures and to thawing temperatures, completely reliable as a standby device, entirely independent of outside power sources, incapable of leaking, and operable without periodic maintenance"}, {"pat_id": "US-4798239-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the two anti-freezing valves 15 and 16 effectively protect the meter against freezing by virtue of the transfer of heat from soil zones where the collectors 10 are buried, to the valves 15 and 16 flanking the meter, thereby preventing the freezing of the water circulating from the valve 15 to the valve 16, even in the case of a substantially negative temperature of the adjacent atmosphere"}, {"pat_id": "US-5715855-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "description of the invention brief summary of the invention the present invention provides a simple design for a mechanically actuated, temperature-responsive valve that efficiently utilizes the volumetric expansion of freezing water to cause water from an outdoor tap to flow through discharge ports"}, {"pat_id": "US-6003780-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "interruption of water supply pressure, when the main fountain valve 20 is in the off condition, does not result in exposing any portion of the collected water to freezing temperatures"}, {"pat_id": "US-6021798-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "when the temperature rises above freezing, the sensor is de-actuated to interrupt the flow of electricity from the power source to the solenoid-actuated valve, and thereby close the valve and stop the flow of water therethrough"}, {"pat_id": "US-6763845-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "indeed, in some particularly preferred embodiments of this invention, the third valve may be attached to a water utilization device that is located out of doors and therefore exposed to freezing temperatures"}, {"pat_id": "US-7497228-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "because the temperature control valve measured a higher temperature, it would remain closed and not allow warmer water from below ground to replace the freezing water"}, {"pat_id": "KR-100385593-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "of course, the effective treatment to remove various heavy metals and salts is made safely and the high-temperature, high-pressure steam generated during the hydrolysis process reaches the predetermined level, and the electronic opening and closing valve 105 is opened in the steam storage chamber 2 separately installed"}, {"pat_id": "US-4922233-A", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "monitoring systems presently used to monitor the condition of a drain valve and employing differential temperature sensors are ineffective or insufficient for a number of reasons"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3983776-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "for example, the smart water valve 126 can determine that the temperature of the water leak of 60 degrees f matches the temperature of water consumed by the toilet of 177 degrees c (62 degrees f)"}, {"pat_id": "EP-3983776-B1", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "in some examples, the smart water valve 126 can determine that temperature of the water leak matches the temperature of the particular water consuming device based on the temperatures matching within a threshold variance"}, {"pat_id": "US-9752787-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "the drain pipe allows for any water that may build up in, or leak into, the valve box to drain away before it can change to steam under the high temperature conditions and cause damage"}, {"pat_id": "US-10537921-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "reference symbol 21 designates a filter unit, reference symbol 23 designates a temperature sensor, reference symbol 25 designates a level sensor, reference symbol 30 designates an object loading unit, reference symbol 31 designates a door lifting drive unit, reference symbol 33 designates a washing lifting drive unit, reference symbol 11 designates spray nozzles, reference symbol 13 designates spray pipelines, reference symbol 15 designates a manual valve, and reference symbol 17 designates electronic valves"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102440380-B1", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "this is because when the temperature drops to sub-zero range in winter, rupture due to freezing in valves or pipes may occur"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102081866-B1", "para_id": "para_2", "text": "in order to avoid the use of expensive sensors necessary to withstand the temperature rise of the evaporator / condenser 4002, pressure sensors p e and p c correspond to the low temperature side of the heat exchanger 4004 and control valves v e and v c ) can be mounted on the fluid line"}, {"pat_id": "US-10914393-B2", "para_id": "para_1", "text": "conventional hot water balancing systems and shutoff valves have centered on the timely delivery of hot water without wasting water while waiting for hot water to arrive to a user, or avoiding excessive energy usage by recirculation pumps, or avoiding scalding a user by limiting the exposure to water above a safe temperature"}, {"pat_id": "KR-102196538-B1", "para_id": "para_6", "text": "it relates to a seismic valve chamber 100 for preventing water accumulation to collect condensation caused by a temperature difference between a chamber, a pipe, and the underground, and water storage due to water loss in a pipe when a facility is replaced"}, {"pat_id": "US-11035484-B2", "para_id": "para_3", "text": "practically, however, it is very difficult to reduce the cross section to zero due to production tolerances on the valve bore and the valve bodies and dimensional changes in operation due to temperature influences and/or wear"}]</data>
